      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-02 (run 20260801-171149) \u2014 integration_definitions (NEW): the tenant-scoped\ndefinition tier. _id IS sha256(JSON.stringify([orgId, key])) \u2014 the deterministic-id insert IS the\n(orgId,key) uniqueness primitive (the data layer has no unique indexes). visibility private|org|global;\nglobal is super-admin-only in BOTH directions, and publishing launches from org so demotion is reversible.\nautomations._id for a MANAGED (package-provisioned) row is now sha256(JSON.stringify([orgId,\nintegrationKey, templateKey])) \u2014 org-scoped, closing the bug where the first org to provision a package\nowned the row and every other org silently got nothing. LEGACY rows keep the old unscoped id and are\nfound by source.{integrationKey,templateKey} provenance, never by _id (see decisions.md 2026-08-02,\nreview 2026-11-01). sync_state / sync_reports (NEW): per-action completeness cursor + run reports.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-02 (run 20260801-171149) \u2014 integration_definitions (NEW): the tenant-scoped\ndefinition tier. _id IS sha256(JSON.stringify([orgId, key])) \u2014 the deterministic-id insert IS the\n(orgId,key) uniqueness primitive (the data layer has no unique indexes). visibility private|org|global;\nglobal is super-admin-only in BOTH directions, and publishing launches from org so demotion is reversible.\nautomations._id for a MANAGED (package-provisioned) row is now sha256(JSON.stringify([orgId,\nintegrationKey, templateKey])) \u2014 org-scoped, closing the bug where the first org to provision a package\nowned the row and every other org silently got nothing. LEGACY rows keep the old unscoped id and are\nfound by source.{integrationKey,templateKey} provenance, never by _id (see decisions.md 2026-08-02,\nreview 2026-11-01). sync_state / sync_reports (NEW): per-action completeness cursor + run reports.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-02 (run 20260801-171149) \u2014 integration_definitions (NEW): the tenant-scoped\ndefinition tier. _id IS sha256(JSON.stringify([orgId, key])) \u2014 the deterministic-id insert IS the\n(orgId,key) uniqueness primitive (the data layer has no unique indexes). visibility private|org|global;\nglobal is super-admin-only in BOTH directions, and publishing launches from org so demotion is reversible.\nautomations._id for a MANAGED (package-provisioned) row is now sha256(JSON.stringify([orgId,\nintegrationKey, templateKey])) \u2014 org-scoped, closing the bug where the first org to provision a package\nowned the row and every other org silently got nothing. LEGACY rows keep the old unscoped id and are\nfound by source.{integrationKey,templateKey} provenance, never by _id (see decisions.md 2026-08-02,\nreview 2026-11-01). sync_state / sync_reports (NEW): per-action completeness cursor + run reports.",
