      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice C2) - NEW COLLECTION approved_integration_actions.\nThe durable record of a human answering \"may this integration action write on my behalf\". Sibling of\napproved_commands (which answers the same question for a command shape on the user's machine); a separate\ncollection because the two are read on different rails by different tiers.\nDOC: { _id, orgId, userId, integrationKey, actionName, shape, decision: 'once'|'always', target, createdAt,\nexpiresAt, lastUsedAt? }. _id = sha256(JSON [orgId, userId, integrationKey, actionName, shape, decision]) - a\nJSON tuple, not a separator join, because every component is a caller-influenced string and a '-' or '::' join\nis not injective when a component may contain the separator (the C1 provisioner-id lesson).\nSCOPE = THE KEY. An approval is not transferable across tenant, user, integration, action or SHAPE, and each\nrefusal has its own test. `shape` is the fingerprint of the action's executable content (backing, transport,\nHTTP method/URL/headers/body template, or the automation binding) - so a re-authored action does not inherit\nthe approval the human gave the old one. Canonicalised (keys sorted at every depth) so a Mongo round trip that\nreorders keys cannot silently invalidate a live approval.\nTTL: 'always' = 90 days (approved_commands' constant). 'once' = 15 minutes AND single-use - the claim is an\natomic findOneAndDelete, so two concurrent runs cannot both spend it. A row with NO expiresAt is treated as\nEXPIRED, never as permanent.\nNO SECRET LIVES HERE: `target` is the rendered destination of the action (already public in the definition's\nown config), never a credential, never an argument value.\nintegration_configs is unchanged by this slice; the credential rotation write on the execution rail now keeps\ncofreItemId + the item's value in step with credentialsCiphertext instead of writing only the latter.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice C2) - NEW COLLECTION approved_integration_actions.\nThe durable record of a human answering \"may this integration action write on my behalf\". Sibling of\napproved_commands (which answers the same question for a command shape on the user's machine); a separate\ncollection because the two are read on different rails by different tiers.\nDOC: { _id, orgId, userId, integrationKey, actionName, shape, decision: 'once'|'always', target, createdAt,\nexpiresAt, lastUsedAt? }. _id = sha256(JSON [orgId, userId, integrationKey, actionName, shape, decision]) - a\nJSON tuple, not a separator join, because every component is a caller-influenced string and a '-' or '::' join\nis not injective when a component may contain the separator (the C1 provisioner-id lesson).\nSCOPE = THE KEY. An approval is not transferable across tenant, user, integration, action or SHAPE, and each\nrefusal has its own test. `shape` is the fingerprint of the action's executable content (backing, transport,\nHTTP method/URL/headers/body template, or the automation binding) - so a re-authored action does not inherit\nthe approval the human gave the old one. Canonicalised (keys sorted at every depth) so a Mongo round trip that\nreorders keys cannot silently invalidate a live approval.\nTTL: 'always' = 90 days (approved_commands' constant). 'once' = 15 minutes AND single-use - the claim is an\natomic findOneAndDelete, so two concurrent runs cannot both spend it. A row with NO expiresAt is treated as\nEXPIRED, never as permanent.\nNO SECRET LIVES HERE: `target` is the rendered destination of the action (already public in the definition's\nown config), never a credential, never an argument value.\nintegration_configs is unchanged by this slice; the credential rotation write on the execution rail now keeps\ncofreItemId + the item's value in step with credentialsCiphertext instead of writing only the latter.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
