    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 660100201,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260803-cs6-citius-sync-plane",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 5160,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 940,
      "height": 620,
      "seed": 660100201,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice CS6) - THE CITIUS SYNC PLANE: two CS3 collections\nput to work plus ONE new collection, all metadata-only.\n\nsync_state (CS3, now written for real by the Citius rail) - one row per LOGICAL SYNC.\n  _id = sha256(JSON [orgId, integrationKey, actionKey]); { watermark: string|null, seenRefs[{ref,itemDate}],\n  lastRunAt?, lastOutcome? 'complete'|'incomplete'|'failed', consecutiveIncomplete, consecutiveFailures,\n  lastError? }. The WATERMARK ADVANCES ONLY ON A PROVED-COMPLETE RUN; a proved-partial run absorbs the refs\n  and leaves the cursor where it is, so the window re-sweeps.\n\n  ONE ORG IS NOT ONE INBOX. Caixa Citius credentials are PER MANDATARIO, so legal/citius-sync.ts composes\n  actionKey = JSON.stringify([baseActionKey, actor.userId]) - two lawyers in one firm get two state rows.\n  Sharing one would let a colleague's complete sweep advance the cursor past notifications this user has\n  never seen: a silent miss with no machinery failure anywhere. JSON, not a '::' join, because a separator\n  join is not injective (the same argument syncStateId's own docblock makes).\n\nsync_reports (CS3) - capped per-key history (50) of SyncRunReport, _id = report id, stateKey = the sync_state\n  _id. Read back by readCitiusSyncState() and safeParse'd against the shared contract before it is served;\n  a row written by an older shape is DROPPED, never handed out as if it validated.\n\ncitius_notifications (NEW, module-local Store in legal/citius-sync.ts - the cofre/store.ts pattern: one\n  writer, one reader, both in that file).\n  _id = sha256(JSON [orgId, integrationKey, actionKey, ref]) - the SAME tuple sync_state hashes, plus the\n  row's dedup ref, so a deterministic-id insert IS the idempotence CS3's land contract requires (insert\n  returns false ONLY for a duplicate key and rethrows everything else, so a transient failure ends the run\n  'failed' with nothing moved rather than marking an unlanded ref as seen).\n  DOC: { _id, orgId, integrationKey, actionKey, ref, itemDate, landedAt, notificacao: {...CitiusNotificacaoMeta} }.\n\n  METADATA ONLY, and the storage shape is HOW that is proven structurally: the parsed record is stored by\n  SPREADING it, so citius-sync.ts contains no documentoRef / docId / Documento identifier anywhere to\n  dereference. The row records that a document EXISTS and holds the inert captured reference; NO DOCUMENT\n  BYTES ARE EVER STORED and no document is ever fetched (zero-hit suite, non-vacuous).",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 660100401,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260803-cs8-lessons-and-graduation",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 5820,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1000,
      "height": 800,
      "seed": 660100401,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice CS8) - THE CITIUS SYNC PLANE, part 2: ONE new\ncollection, one read lifted to where the data is, and one silent-miss DEFECT removed from the plane.\n\nsync_lessons (NEW, module-local Store in events/sync-lessons.ts - the same one-writer-one-reader pattern\n  citius_notifications uses; not in data/stores.ts).\n  _id = sha256(JSON [ syncStateId(key), kind, signature ]) - the SAME identity sync_state and sync_reports\n  are keyed by, PLUS the fact. DOC: { _id, stateKey, orgId, integrationKey, actionKey, kind, signature,\n  detail, page?, firstSeenAt, lastSeenAt, occurrences, lastReportId?, lastOutcome? }.\n  kind = parse | pager | session | transport | completeness.\n\n  KNOWLEDGE, NOT A LOG, and that IS the storage shape: the row is keyed by the FACT, so the same portal\n  quirk met on 200 polls is ONE row with occurrences:200 and an immutable firstSeenAt. sync_reports is\n  already the per-run trail; a second one would add nothing. Bounded twice, because part of a signature\n  comes from source-controlled text: signature/detail truncated + digit runs collapsed to '#' (so a\n  varying timeout is one fact), <=25 distinct lessons per run, <=200 rows per key (least-recently-seen\n  pruned, warned).\n\n  PER-ACTOR like everything else on this plane: stateKey = syncStateId(key) and key.actionKey carries the\n  mandatario, so two lawyers in one firm keep two bodies of knowledge and neither read sees the other.\n  syncStateId now FAILS CLOSED on a blank component, so an unscoped key reaches none of the three\n  collections at all.\n\n  METADATA ONLY holds here too: lessons are derived from a walk's STATUS fields (status, incomplete\n  reason, per-page outcome/note/status) and never from its ROWS, so no processo, no ref and above all no\n  document reference can reach this collection. Pinned with a non-vacuous test (the same run's landed\n  rows DO carry document references).\n\nsync_reports - the \"latest report\" read GRADUATED out of legal/citius-sync.ts into\n  events/sync-state.ts#latestSyncReport(key), where the collection lives. Semantics, stated once:\n  LATEST = greatest startedAt (by START, not end), tie-broken deterministically by endedAt then _id -\n  a fixed clock makes ties routine, and an unbroken tie makes the read answer differently on two calls.\n  NONE = undefined. STALE SHAPE = safeParse'd and DROPPED, and deliberately NOT backfilled from the next\n  valid row: 'latest' names THE MOST RECENT RUN, and an older report served under that name would\n  contradict the state row's own lastOutcome.\n\nsync_state - advanceWatermark is now MONOTONIC: a proposed watermark strictly OLDER than the stored one\n  is refused (only when both parse as instants - the cursor is documented opaque). A backwards clock must\n  not re-open a window that was already proved swept.\n\nDEFECT REMOVED FROM THIS PLANE (CS6 review, fixed CS8): legal/citius-sync.ts filtered enumerated rows by\n  itemDate >= watermark. The watermark is a WALL-CLOCK instant; a date-only portal cell normalises to\n  MIDNIGHT UTC. A notification dated the same day as the last complete run therefore sat BELOW the cursor,\n  was dropped from BOTH passes, the passes agreed, the run was certified 'complete' and the cursor\n  advanced past a row that had never landed and never could. The filter is GONE: every captured row is\n  handed to runVerifiedSync, which dedups by REFERENCE (exact) and lands idempotently by deterministic id.\n  window.since remains on the report as evidence only.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice CS8) - THE CITIUS SYNC PLANE, part 2: ONE new\ncollection, one read lifted to where the data is, and one silent-miss DEFECT removed from the plane.\n\nsync_lessons (NEW, module-local Store in events/sync-lessons.ts - the same one-writer-one-reader pattern\n  citius_notifications uses; not in data/stores.ts).\n  _id = sha256(JSON [ syncStateId(key), kind, signature ]) - the SAME identity sync_state and sync_reports\n  are keyed by, PLUS the fact. DOC: { _id, stateKey, orgId, integrationKey, actionKey, kind, signature,\n  detail, page?, firstSeenAt, lastSeenAt, occurrences, lastReportId?, lastOutcome? }.\n  kind = parse | pager | session | transport | completeness.\n\n  KNOWLEDGE, NOT A LOG, and that IS the storage shape: the row is keyed by the FACT, so the same portal\n  quirk met on 200 polls is ONE row with occurrences:200 and an immutable firstSeenAt. sync_reports is\n  already the per-run trail; a second one would add nothing. Bounded twice, because part of a signature\n  comes from source-controlled text: signature/detail truncated + digit runs collapsed to '#' (so a\n  varying timeout is one fact), <=25 distinct lessons per run, <=200 rows per key (least-recently-seen\n  pruned, warned).\n\n  PER-ACTOR like everything else on this plane: stateKey = syncStateId(key) and key.actionKey carries the\n  mandatario, so two lawyers in one firm keep two bodies of knowledge and neither read sees the other.\n  syncStateId now FAILS CLOSED on a blank component, so an unscoped key reaches none of the three\n  collections at all.\n\n  METADATA ONLY holds here too: lessons are derived from a walk's STATUS fields (status, incomplete\n  reason, per-page outcome/note/status) and never from its ROWS, so no processo, no ref and above all no\n  document reference can reach this collection. Pinned with a non-vacuous test (the same run's landed\n  rows DO carry document references).\n\nsync_reports - the \"latest report\" read GRADUATED out of legal/citius-sync.ts into\n  events/sync-state.ts#latestSyncReport(key), where the collection lives. Semantics, stated once:\n  LATEST = greatest startedAt (by START, not end), tie-broken deterministically by endedAt then _id -\n  a fixed clock makes ties routine, and an unbroken tie makes the read answer differently on two calls.\n  NONE = undefined. STALE SHAPE = safeParse'd and DROPPED, and deliberately NOT backfilled from the next\n  valid row: 'latest' names THE MOST RECENT RUN, and an older report served under that name would\n  contradict the state row's own lastOutcome.\n\nsync_state - advanceWatermark is now MONOTONIC: a proposed watermark strictly OLDER than the stored one\n  is refused (only when both parse as instants - the cursor is documented opaque). A backwards clock must\n  not re-open a window that was already proved swept.\n\nDEFECT REMOVED FROM THIS PLANE (CS6 review, fixed CS8): legal/citius-sync.ts filtered enumerated rows by\n  itemDate >= watermark. The watermark is a WALL-CLOCK instant; a date-only portal cell normalises to\n  MIDNIGHT UTC. A notification dated the same day as the last complete run therefore sat BELOW the cursor,\n  was dropped from BOTH passes, the passes agreed, the run was certified 'complete' and the cursor\n  advanced past a row that had never landed and never could. The filter is GONE: every captured row is\n  handed to runVerifiedSync, which dedups by REFERENCE (exact) and lands idempotently by deterministic id.\n  window.since remains on the report as evidence only."
    },
