      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice D1) - WHAT THE PUBLIC CAPABILITY SURFACE READS AND WRITES.\n\nNO NEW COLLECTION. The capability surface is a READ + EXECUTE projection over collections that already\nexist; it introduces no storage of its own.\n\nREADS\n  integration_definitions   through definition-registry.resolveDefinition / listDefinitionsFor, ALWAYS\n                            under the actor built from the verified principal (A1's visibility gate).\n                            The projection is definitionFromDoc's, unchanged: the storage envelope is\n                            dropped, _id + visibility appear ONLY for a row of the caller's own org, and\n                            redactSecrets runs on both tiers - so a cross-org 'global' row reaches a\n                            capability client with no author, no id and no pasted credential.\n  integration_configs       findConfigForOwner(orgId, ownerUserId, key) - the SAME lookup the executor\n                            performs, so the reported 'connected' cannot drift from what an execute does.\n  approved_integration_actions  liveApprovalFor(...) - READ ONLY, and advisory: the gate is re-evaluated\n                            inside the executor at call time, where a 'once' row is atomically CLAIMED.\n                            The capability rail never writes this collection.\n\nWRITES\n  activity_logs             ONE row per execute, category 'integrations', type 'capability_execute',\n                            under BOTH admissions (an execute has side effects on a third-party account,\n                            so the trail must not depend on what admitted it). Metadata carries\n                            integrationKey / actionName / verdict / code / status / ms and, for a\n                            key-admitted call, keyId + the capped trace-only x-client tag. It carries\n                            NEITHER the request args NOR the response data: an audit trail that copies\n                            the payload is a new exfiltration surface, not a control.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice D1) - WHAT THE PUBLIC CAPABILITY SURFACE READS AND WRITES.\n\nNO NEW COLLECTION. The capability surface is a READ + EXECUTE projection over collections that already\nexist; it introduces no storage of its own.\n\nREADS\n  integration_definitions   through definition-registry.resolveDefinition / listDefinitionsFor, ALWAYS\n                            under the actor built from the verified principal (A1's visibility gate).\n                            The projection is definitionFromDoc's, unchanged: the storage envelope is\n                            dropped, _id + visibility appear ONLY for a row of the caller's own org, and\n                            redactSecrets runs on both tiers - so a cross-org 'global' row reaches a\n                            capability client with no author, no id and no pasted credential.\n  integration_configs       findConfigForOwner(orgId, ownerUserId, key) - the SAME lookup the executor\n                            performs, so the reported 'connected' cannot drift from what an execute does.\n  approved_integration_actions  liveApprovalFor(...) - READ ONLY, and advisory: the gate is re-evaluated\n                            inside the executor at call time, where a 'once' row is atomically CLAIMED.\n                            The capability rail never writes this collection.\n\nWRITES\n  activity_logs             ONE row per execute, category 'integrations', type 'capability_execute',\n                            under BOTH admissions (an execute has side effects on a third-party account,\n                            so the trail must not depend on what admitted it). Metadata carries\n                            integrationKey / actionName / verdict / code / status / ms and, for a\n                            key-admitted call, keyId + the capped trace-only x-client tag. It carries\n                            NEITHER the request args NOR the response data: an audit trail that copies\n                            the payload is a new exfiltration surface, not a control.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice D1) - WHAT THE PUBLIC CAPABILITY SURFACE READS AND WRITES.\n\nNO NEW COLLECTION. The capability surface is a READ + EXECUTE projection over collections that already\nexist; it introduces no storage of its own.\n\nREADS\n  integration_definitions   through definition-registry.resolveDefinition / listDefinitionsFor, ALWAYS\n                            under the actor built from the verified principal (A1's visibility gate).\n                            The projection is definitionFromDoc's, unchanged: the storage envelope is\n                            dropped, _id + visibility appear ONLY for a row of the caller's own org, and\n                            redactSecrets runs on both tiers - so a cross-org 'global' row reaches a\n                            capability client with no author, no id and no pasted credential.\n  integration_configs       findConfigForOwner(orgId, ownerUserId, key) - the SAME lookup the executor\n                            performs, so the reported 'connected' cannot drift from what an execute does.\n  approved_integration_actions  liveApprovalFor(...) - READ ONLY, and advisory: the gate is re-evaluated\n                            inside the executor at call time, where a 'once' row is atomically CLAIMED.\n                            The capability rail never writes this collection.\n\nWRITES\n  activity_logs             ONE row per execute, category 'integrations', type 'capability_execute',\n                            under BOTH admissions (an execute has side effects on a third-party account,\n                            so the trail must not depend on what admitted it). Metadata carries\n                            integrationKey / actionName / verdict / code / status / ms and, for a\n                            key-admitted call, keyId + the capped trace-only x-client tag. It carries\n                            NEITHER the request args NOR the response data: an audit trail that copies\n                            the payload is a new exfiltration surface, not a control.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 812340001,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260803-e2-publish-snapshot",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 7275,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 980,
      "height": 676,
      "seed": 812340001,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice E2) - THE FROZEN PUBLISHED SNAPSHOT.\nintegration_definitions gains TWO fields; no new collection.\n\npublishedSnapshot { scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy, scrubVersion, config, skillMd, lessons?, modelPass\n  {status:'applied'|'skipped'|'failed', reason?, spansApplied?}, redactionCount,\n  supersedes?{scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy} }\n  ONE field = ONE live snapshot. A re-publish REPLACES it wholesale and stamps `supersedes` with\n  the replaced one - that IS the supersede protocol; there is no version chain to choose between.\n  No separate snapshots collection, on A1's reasoning for actions[] being inline: it has no\n  lifecycle apart from its definition, and a second doc is a second thing that can be missing.\n  WRITTEN ONLY by IntegrationDefinitionStore.publishSnapshot, in the SAME gated CAS write that\n  sets visibility:'global' - a published row and its scrubbed artifact cannot disagree.\n  PRESERVED by create(onConflict:'replace'): a content write must not silently return a published\n  row to serving its LIVE bytes cross-org.\n\npublishRequest { requestedBy, requestedAt, note? }\n  The AUTHOR-INITIATED submit-for-review state (closes the E1 review's deferred F2). Presence is\n  the ONLY thing that makes an `org` row visible to a super-admin who is not a member of the org;\n  a `private` row is never submittable. Survives publication so publish/un-publish stay inverse.\n  Review queue = listPublishRequests (super-admin), its own surface, NOT folded into listForActor.\n\nREAD DIRECTION (definition-registry.crossOrgView): a row of ANOTHER org - which the A1 gate means\nis always `global` - is projected from publishedSnapshot; with no snapshot, through the\ndeterministic publish FLOOR at read time. Own-org rows are untouched. This is the single point\nevery reader passes, INCLUDING the credential-egress origin resolver, so a consuming org's\nallow-list is the reviewed artifact's baseUrls and not the author's live ones.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice E2) - THE FROZEN PUBLISHED SNAPSHOT.\nintegration_definitions gains TWO fields; no new collection.\n\npublishedSnapshot { scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy, scrubVersion, config, skillMd, lessons?, modelPass\n  {status:'applied'|'skipped'|'failed', reason?, spansApplied?}, redactionCount,\n  supersedes?{scrubbedAt, scrubbedBy} }\n  ONE field = ONE live snapshot. A re-publish REPLACES it wholesale and stamps `supersedes` with\n  the replaced one - that IS the supersede protocol; there is no version chain to choose between.\n  No separate snapshots collection, on A1's reasoning for actions[] being inline: it has no\n  lifecycle apart from its definition, and a second doc is a second thing that can be missing.\n  WRITTEN ONLY by IntegrationDefinitionStore.publishSnapshot, in the SAME gated CAS write that\n  sets visibility:'global' - a published row and its scrubbed artifact cannot disagree.\n  PRESERVED by create(onConflict:'replace'): a content write must not silently return a published\n  row to serving its LIVE bytes cross-org.\n\npublishRequest { requestedBy, requestedAt, note? }\n  The AUTHOR-INITIATED submit-for-review state (closes the E1 review's deferred F2). Presence is\n  the ONLY thing that makes an `org` row visible to a super-admin who is not a member of the org;\n  a `private` row is never submittable. Survives publication so publish/un-publish stay inverse.\n  Review queue = listPublishRequests (super-admin), its own surface, NOT folded into listForActor.\n\nREAD DIRECTION (definition-registry.crossOrgView): a row of ANOTHER org - which the A1 gate means\nis always `global` - is projected from publishedSnapshot; with no snapshot, through the\ndeterministic publish FLOOR at read time. Own-org rows are untouched. This is the single point\nevery reader passes, INCLUDING the credential-egress origin resolver, so a consuming org's\nallow-list is the reviewed artifact's baseUrls and not the author's live ones.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
