      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, review of B2+C2) - integration_configs GAINS custodianUserId.\n\nWHY THE FIELD EXISTS. ownerUserId answers \"who may USE this config\" and is UNDEFINED for an org-shared\nrow by construction, so it cannot answer \"whose authority GOVERNS this credential\". Something has to,\nbecause an integration definition resolves per (key, PRINCIPAL) - definition-store getForActor answers\nthe reader's own `private` row before any org/global/baseline one - and both credential rails were\nresolving it as the READER. For an org-shared config that let a same-org peer (role `user`) PUT their\nown package under the key and thereby author BOTH the action that runs AND the hosts the org-admin's\ncredential may be sent to. Probed to {\"success\":true} with a live key on exfil.example, on the action\nexecutor rail and on the automation api_call rail. findings.md\n`org-shared-credential-egress-was-authored-by-the-reader`.\n\nTHE FIELD. custodianUserId = the user whose credential-typing CEREMONY produced the bundle the row\ncurrently holds. Stamped server-side from the verified actor by service.createConfig and by a\ncredential-bearing service.updateConfig (both already canWriteConfig-gated); never from a request body;\nnever on configSummary, so it is not wire-visible; and NEVER moved by a provider rotation.\n\nHOW IT IS READ. credential-cofre.definitionActorForCredential(reader, config) is the one rule:\n  no config           -> the reader (no credential at stake)\n  ownerUserId set     -> its owner, which findConfigForOwner guarantees IS the reader (role preserved)\n  org-shared, stamped -> the custodian\n  org-shared, absent  -> systemActorForOrg(orgId): org + global + baseline, never a user's private row\n                         (the fail-closed shape for rows written before the stamp; a re-save fixes it)\n  incoherent          -> null, i.e. REFUSE. An org-less actor matches every `global` row (A2 F4), so\n                         \"cannot determine the custodian\" must never become \"resolve as somebody\".\nUsed for the ACTION resolution and the EGRESS ALLOW-LIST alike, from\ncredential-cofre.resolveCredentialEgressBinding - one rule, granted | refused | unbound, projected by\nboth rails (the api_call seam has no unbound branch; assertOriginAllowed refuses an empty list).\n\nROTATION CUSTODY (same review). mintOrRefreshCredentialShadow takes ceremony | rotation. The rotation\nmode has NO mint branch, passes an empty boundOrigins so rewriteValue cannot re-bind, never re-grants\nand never re-stamps custodianUserId. Before it, a STALE JOIN (the item deleted out from under the row)\nminted a fresh auto-granted until_locked item holding the admin's bundle in the RUNNING user's Cofre\nand re-stamped cofreItemId - custody, and the lock switch, moved to whoever happened to be running.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, review of B2+C2) - integration_configs GAINS custodianUserId.\n\nWHY THE FIELD EXISTS. ownerUserId answers \"who may USE this config\" and is UNDEFINED for an org-shared\nrow by construction, so it cannot answer \"whose authority GOVERNS this credential\". Something has to,\nbecause an integration definition resolves per (key, PRINCIPAL) - definition-store getForActor answers\nthe reader's own `private` row before any org/global/baseline one - and both credential rails were\nresolving it as the READER. For an org-shared config that let a same-org peer (role `user`) PUT their\nown package under the key and thereby author BOTH the action that runs AND the hosts the org-admin's\ncredential may be sent to. Probed to {\"success\":true} with a live key on exfil.example, on the action\nexecutor rail and on the automation api_call rail. findings.md\n`org-shared-credential-egress-was-authored-by-the-reader`.\n\nTHE FIELD. custodianUserId = the user whose credential-typing CEREMONY produced the bundle the row\ncurrently holds. Stamped server-side from the verified actor by service.createConfig and by a\ncredential-bearing service.updateConfig (both already canWriteConfig-gated); never from a request body;\nnever on configSummary, so it is not wire-visible; and NEVER moved by a provider rotation.\n\nHOW IT IS READ. credential-cofre.definitionActorForCredential(reader, config) is the one rule:\n  no config           -> the reader (no credential at stake)\n  ownerUserId set     -> its owner, which findConfigForOwner guarantees IS the reader (role preserved)\n  org-shared, stamped -> the custodian\n  org-shared, absent  -> systemActorForOrg(orgId): org + global + baseline, never a user's private row\n                         (the fail-closed shape for rows written before the stamp; a re-save fixes it)\n  incoherent          -> null, i.e. REFUSE. An org-less actor matches every `global` row (A2 F4), so\n                         \"cannot determine the custodian\" must never become \"resolve as somebody\".\nUsed for the ACTION resolution and the EGRESS ALLOW-LIST alike, from\ncredential-cofre.resolveCredentialEgressBinding - one rule, granted | refused | unbound, projected by\nboth rails (the api_call seam has no unbound branch; assertOriginAllowed refuses an empty list).\n\nROTATION CUSTODY (same review). mintOrRefreshCredentialShadow takes ceremony | rotation. The rotation\nmode has NO mint branch, passes an empty boundOrigins so rewriteValue cannot re-bind, never re-grants\nand never re-stamps custodianUserId. Before it, a STALE JOIN (the item deleted out from under the row)\nminted a fresh auto-granted until_locked item holding the admin's bundle in the RUNNING user's Cofre\nand re-stamped cofreItemId - custody, and the lock switch, moved to whoever happened to be running.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, review of B2+C2) - integration_configs GAINS custodianUserId.\n\nWHY THE FIELD EXISTS. ownerUserId answers \"who may USE this config\" and is UNDEFINED for an org-shared\nrow by construction, so it cannot answer \"whose authority GOVERNS this credential\". Something has to,\nbecause an integration definition resolves per (key, PRINCIPAL) - definition-store getForActor answers\nthe reader's own `private` row before any org/global/baseline one - and both credential rails were\nresolving it as the READER. For an org-shared config that let a same-org peer (role `user`) PUT their\nown package under the key and thereby author BOTH the action that runs AND the hosts the org-admin's\ncredential may be sent to. Probed to {\"success\":true} with a live key on exfil.example, on the action\nexecutor rail and on the automation api_call rail. findings.md\n`org-shared-credential-egress-was-authored-by-the-reader`.\n\nTHE FIELD. custodianUserId = the user whose credential-typing CEREMONY produced the bundle the row\ncurrently holds. Stamped server-side from the verified actor by service.createConfig and by a\ncredential-bearing service.updateConfig (both already canWriteConfig-gated); never from a request body;\nnever on configSummary, so it is not wire-visible; and NEVER moved by a provider rotation.\n\nHOW IT IS READ. credential-cofre.definitionActorForCredential(reader, config) is the one rule:\n  no config           -> the reader (no credential at stake)\n  ownerUserId set     -> its owner, which findConfigForOwner guarantees IS the reader (role preserved)\n  org-shared, stamped -> the custodian\n  org-shared, absent  -> systemActorForOrg(orgId): org + global + baseline, never a user's private row\n                         (the fail-closed shape for rows written before the stamp; a re-save fixes it)\n  incoherent          -> null, i.e. REFUSE. An org-less actor matches every `global` row (A2 F4), so\n                         \"cannot determine the custodian\" must never become \"resolve as somebody\".\nUsed for the ACTION resolution and the EGRESS ALLOW-LIST alike, from\ncredential-cofre.resolveCredentialEgressBinding - one rule, granted | refused | unbound, projected by\nboth rails (the api_call seam has no unbound branch; assertOriginAllowed refuses an empty list).\n\nROTATION CUSTODY (same review). mintOrRefreshCredentialShadow takes ceremony | rotation. The rotation\nmode has NO mint branch, passes an empty boundOrigins so rewriteValue cannot re-bind, never re-grants\nand never re-stamps custodianUserId. Before it, a STALE JOIN (the item deleted out from under the row)\nminted a fresh auto-granted until_locked item holding the admin's bundle in the RUNNING user's Cofre\nand re-stamped cofreItemId - custody, and the lock switch, moved to whoever happened to be running.",
