      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice C3) - integration_definitions.lessons BECOMES A\nFIRST-CLASS EDITABLE FIELD. No new collection, no new field: the column already existed (carried by\ndefinition-save and by E2's publishableContentOf); C3 gives it a read, a write and a prompt route.\n\nTHE FIELD. lessons?: string on integration_definitions - free text an operator records about what an\nintegration taught them. Bounded at INTEGRATION_LESSONS_MAX_CHARS = 20_000 (shared/src/integrations.ts),\nONE constant behind the zod .max(), the api seam's own check and the dashboard counter. The ceiling is a\nREFUSAL, never a truncation: a trimmed note is worse than a rejected one, because the author believes it\nwas recorded.\n\nTWO PROJECTIONS OF ONE STORED VALUE (definition-lessons.ts#lessonsViewOf):\n  canEditDefinitionRaw(doc, actor) -> BYTE-EXACT, editable:true. The SAVE path's own admission set, so\n    the raw view is worth exactly what the save that follows it is worth (D2 re-review HIGH-1). Without\n    it an edit cycle round-trips a redaction into stored documentation (A3 review F3).\n  otherwise                        -> crossOrgView(doc, actor) then scrubSecretText, editable:false.\nThe PROMPT view (lessonsForPrompt) is scrubbed UNCONDITIONALLY - for the author too - because that side\nis model egress and the raw view exists only to protect an edit round trip (A2 review F7 floor).\n\nCROSS-ORG IS E2's RULE, NOT A SECOND ONE. crossOrgView -> publishedViewOf: with a snapshot the reader\ngets the SNAPSHOT's lessons; a snapshot that PREDATES the lessons yields lessons: undefined, i.e. a\nforeign org sees NOTHING until a re-publish. Without a snapshot, the deterministic publish floor runs at\nread time. Frozen means frozen in both directions.\n\nTHE WRITE IS COMPARE-AND-SWAP. IntegrationDefinitionStore.setLessons(id, actor, lessons, {admit,\nexpectedUpdatedAt}) - the admission predicate is INJECTED (definition-store cannot import the registry\nwithout a cycle), and re-judged INSIDE the CAS mutator against the row actually being written (the E1\nreview F4b re-assert). The token is the ROW's updatedAt, so an unrelated write (a builder save, a\nvisibility flip) also invalidates a pending lessons edit - deliberate: the row you were editing is not\nthe row you loaded. nextStamp() bumps it STRICTLY MONOTONICALLY (max(now, prev+1)), because two writes\ninside one millisecond would otherwise share the very token the CAS exists to bite on. Verdicts:\nok | notfound | forbidden | stale(doc) - stale carries what IS stored, so nothing is guessed or lost.\n\nSCOPE, AS A LIMITATION. Lessons live on STORED rows only. A shipped baseline package has no lessons\nsurface at all (404 both ways, the dashboard renders nothing) - minting a tenant row to shadow a shipped\nkey is what A3's save path refuses by design, so an operator forks first.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice C3) - integration_definitions.lessons BECOMES A\nFIRST-CLASS EDITABLE FIELD. No new collection, no new field: the column already existed (carried by\ndefinition-save and by E2's publishableContentOf); C3 gives it a read, a write and a prompt route.\n\nTHE FIELD. lessons?: string on integration_definitions - free text an operator records about what an\nintegration taught them. Bounded at INTEGRATION_LESSONS_MAX_CHARS = 20_000 (shared/src/integrations.ts),\nONE constant behind the zod .max(), the api seam's own check and the dashboard counter. The ceiling is a\nREFUSAL, never a truncation: a trimmed note is worse than a rejected one, because the author believes it\nwas recorded.\n\nTWO PROJECTIONS OF ONE STORED VALUE (definition-lessons.ts#lessonsViewOf):\n  canEditDefinitionRaw(doc, actor) -> BYTE-EXACT, editable:true. The SAVE path's own admission set, so\n    the raw view is worth exactly what the save that follows it is worth (D2 re-review HIGH-1). Without\n    it an edit cycle round-trips a redaction into stored documentation (A3 review F3).\n  otherwise                        -> crossOrgView(doc, actor) then scrubSecretText, editable:false.\nThe PROMPT view (lessonsForPrompt) is scrubbed UNCONDITIONALLY - for the author too - because that side\nis model egress and the raw view exists only to protect an edit round trip (A2 review F7 floor).\n\nCROSS-ORG IS E2's RULE, NOT A SECOND ONE. crossOrgView -> publishedViewOf: with a snapshot the reader\ngets the SNAPSHOT's lessons; a snapshot that PREDATES the lessons yields lessons: undefined, i.e. a\nforeign org sees NOTHING until a re-publish. Without a snapshot, the deterministic publish floor runs at\nread time. Frozen means frozen in both directions.\n\nTHE WRITE IS COMPARE-AND-SWAP. IntegrationDefinitionStore.setLessons(id, actor, lessons, {admit,\nexpectedUpdatedAt}) - the admission predicate is INJECTED (definition-store cannot import the registry\nwithout a cycle), and re-judged INSIDE the CAS mutator against the row actually being written (the E1\nreview F4b re-assert). The token is the ROW's updatedAt, so an unrelated write (a builder save, a\nvisibility flip) also invalidates a pending lessons edit - deliberate: the row you were editing is not\nthe row you loaded. nextStamp() bumps it STRICTLY MONOTONICALLY (max(now, prev+1)), because two writes\ninside one millisecond would otherwise share the very token the CAS exists to bite on. Verdicts:\nok | notfound | forbidden | stale(doc) - stale carries what IS stored, so nothing is guessed or lost.\n\nSCOPE, AS A LIMITATION. Lessons live on STORED rows only. A shipped baseline package has no lessons\nsurface at all (404 both ways, the dashboard renders nothing) - minting a tenant row to shadow a shipped\nkey is what A3's save path refuses by design, so an operator forks first.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-03 (run 20260801-171149, slice C3) - integration_definitions.lessons BECOMES A\nFIRST-CLASS EDITABLE FIELD. No new collection, no new field: the column already existed (carried by\ndefinition-save and by E2's publishableContentOf); C3 gives it a read, a write and a prompt route.\n\nTHE FIELD. lessons?: string on integration_definitions - free text an operator records about what an\nintegration taught them. Bounded at INTEGRATION_LESSONS_MAX_CHARS = 20_000 (shared/src/integrations.ts),\nONE constant behind the zod .max(), the api seam's own check and the dashboard counter. The ceiling is a\nREFUSAL, never a truncation: a trimmed note is worse than a rejected one, because the author believes it\nwas recorded.\n\nTWO PROJECTIONS OF ONE STORED VALUE (definition-lessons.ts#lessonsViewOf):\n  canEditDefinitionRaw(doc, actor) -> BYTE-EXACT, editable:true. The SAVE path's own admission set, so\n    the raw view is worth exactly what the save that follows it is worth (D2 re-review HIGH-1). Without\n    it an edit cycle round-trips a redaction into stored documentation (A3 review F3).\n  otherwise                        -> crossOrgView(doc, actor) then scrubSecretText, editable:false.\nThe PROMPT view (lessonsForPrompt) is scrubbed UNCONDITIONALLY - for the author too - because that side\nis model egress and the raw view exists only to protect an edit round trip (A2 review F7 floor).\n\nCROSS-ORG IS E2's RULE, NOT A SECOND ONE. crossOrgView -> publishedViewOf: with a snapshot the reader\ngets the SNAPSHOT's lessons; a snapshot that PREDATES the lessons yields lessons: undefined, i.e. a\nforeign org sees NOTHING until a re-publish. Without a snapshot, the deterministic publish floor runs at\nread time. Frozen means frozen in both directions.\n\nTHE WRITE IS COMPARE-AND-SWAP. IntegrationDefinitionStore.setLessons(id, actor, lessons, {admit,\nexpectedUpdatedAt}) - the admission predicate is INJECTED (definition-store cannot import the registry\nwithout a cycle), and re-judged INSIDE the CAS mutator against the row actually being written (the E1\nreview F4b re-assert). The token is the ROW's updatedAt, so an unrelated write (a builder save, a\nvisibility flip) also invalidates a pending lessons edit - deliberate: the row you were editing is not\nthe row you loaded. nextStamp() bumps it STRICTLY MONOTONICALLY (max(now, prev+1)), because two writes\ninside one millisecond would otherwise share the very token the CAS exists to bite on. Verdicts:\nok | notfound | forbidden | stale(doc) - stale carries what IS stored, so nothing is guessed or lost.\n\nSCOPE, AS A LIMITATION. Lessons live on STORED rows only. A shipped baseline package has no lessons\nsurface at all (404 both ways, the dashboard renders nothing) - minting a tenant row to shadow a shipped\nkey is what A3's save path refuses by design, so an operator forks first.",
