      "versionNonce": 208745511,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1754640000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS3, artifact wire contract + continue-flow): artifactView\n(api/src/apps/artifacts-service.ts) gains SIX more narrow top-level lifts off the SAME\nserver-owned data bag as importedFrom/screenshotUrl above - sessionId, outputKind, appUrl,\ndescription, updateAvailable (all data.X, additive per Rule 7, never the bag itself) - plus\nhealth (ROW-level, written by POST /api/app-health, never inside data) and now-populated\ncreatedAt/updatedAt/featuredRank: these three were already on the wire SCHEMA but no code path\nhad ever stamped them, so every artifact card's relative-time label and \"recent first\" sort\nwere dead on arrival.\n\ncreatedAt/updatedAt are now stamped at every creation path (createArtifact, prepareFirstBuild;\nfork/import already had it) and bumped on every mutation that represents real activity\n(patchArtifact, patchArtifactData, build-mechanics activateArtifact on every build completion -\nfirst AND follow-up).\n\nPOST /sessions accepting artifactId (SessionCreateRequest already declared it; no caller had\never passed it) now reciprocally links the ARTIFACT's data.sessionId server-side\n(routes/sessions.ts, through patchArtifactData after a loadWritable check) - the only way it CAN\nbe linked, since sessionId is a RESERVED data key and a client PATCH is stripped of it at the\nroute boundary. This is what makes /chat?continue=<artifactId> resolve to the SAME session on\nevery click instead of silently creating a fresh empty one each time (the bug the operator\nreported as \"clicking to continue an artifact opens a new empty chat\").\n\nScreenshot capture (services/artifact-screenshot.ts) gains a LAZY on-demand backfill:\nGET /artifacts queues (concurrency-capped at 2, deduped per id, EKOA_SCREENSHOTS_DISABLED-gated,\nnever awaited) a capture for any runnable listed artifact with none yet, instead of leaving an\nartifact built before the capture path existed thumbnail-less forever.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS3, artifact wire contract + continue-flow): artifactView\n(api/src/apps/artifacts-service.ts) gains SIX more narrow top-level lifts off the SAME\nserver-owned data bag as importedFrom/screenshotUrl above - sessionId, outputKind, appUrl,\ndescription, updateAvailable (all data.X, additive per Rule 7, never the bag itself) - plus\nhealth (ROW-level, written by POST /api/app-health, never inside data) and now-populated\ncreatedAt/updatedAt/featuredRank: these three were already on the wire SCHEMA but no code path\nhad ever stamped them, so every artifact card's relative-time label and \"recent first\" sort\nwere dead on arrival.\n\ncreatedAt/updatedAt are now stamped at every creation path (createArtifact, prepareFirstBuild;\nfork/import already had it) and bumped on every mutation that represents real activity\n(patchArtifact, patchArtifactData, build-mechanics activateArtifact on every build completion -\nfirst AND follow-up).\n\nPOST /sessions accepting artifactId (SessionCreateRequest already declared it; no caller had\never passed it) now reciprocally links the ARTIFACT's data.sessionId server-side\n(routes/sessions.ts, through patchArtifactData after a loadWritable check) - the only way it CAN\nbe linked, since sessionId is a RESERVED data key and a client PATCH is stripped of it at the\nroute boundary. This is what makes /chat?continue=<artifactId> resolve to the SAME session on\nevery click instead of silently creating a fresh empty one each time (the bug the operator\nreported as \"clicking to continue an artifact opens a new empty chat\").\n\nScreenshot capture (services/artifact-screenshot.ts) gains a LAZY on-demand backfill:\nGET /artifacts queues (concurrency-capped at 2, deduped per id, EKOA_SCREENSHOTS_DISABLED-gated,\nnever awaited) a capture for any runnable listed artifact with none yet, instead of leaving an\nartifact built before the capture path existed thumbnail-less forever.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-08 (WS3, artifact wire contract + continue-flow): artifactView\n(api/src/apps/artifacts-service.ts) gains SIX more narrow top-level lifts off the SAME\nserver-owned data bag as importedFrom/screenshotUrl above - sessionId, outputKind, appUrl,\ndescription, updateAvailable (all data.X, additive per Rule 7, never the bag itself) - plus\nhealth (ROW-level, written by POST /api/app-health, never inside data) and now-populated\ncreatedAt/updatedAt/featuredRank: these three were already on the wire SCHEMA but no code path\nhad ever stamped them, so every artifact card's relative-time label and \"recent first\" sort\nwere dead on arrival.\n\ncreatedAt/updatedAt are now stamped at every creation path (createArtifact, prepareFirstBuild;\nfork/import already had it) and bumped on every mutation that represents real activity\n(patchArtifact, patchArtifactData, build-mechanics activateArtifact on every build completion -\nfirst AND follow-up).\n\nPOST /sessions accepting artifactId (SessionCreateRequest already declared it; no caller had\never passed it) now reciprocally links the ARTIFACT's data.sessionId server-side\n(routes/sessions.ts, through patchArtifactData after a loadWritable check) - the only way it CAN\nbe linked, since sessionId is a RESERVED data key and a client PATCH is stripped of it at the\nroute boundary. This is what makes /chat?continue=<artifactId> resolve to the SAME session on\nevery click instead of silently creating a fresh empty one each time (the bug the operator\nreported as \"clicking to continue an artifact opens a new empty chat\").\n\nScreenshot capture (services/artifact-screenshot.ts) gains a LAZY on-demand backfill:\nGET /artifacts queues (concurrency-capped at 2, deduped per id, EKOA_SCREENSHOTS_DISABLED-gated,\nnever awaited) a capture for any runnable listed artifact with none yet, instead of leaving an\nartifact built before the capture path existed thumbnail-less forever.",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "annot-salomao-trigger-import-2026-08-14",
