      "x": 60,
      "y": 11432.5,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1040,
      "height": 225,
      "seed": 202608174,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755442800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-17 (schedules): TWO new collections (api/src/data/stores.ts). `schedules`\n{_id, orgId, ownerUserId (server-stamped, the fire-time authority), name, description?, target\n(manual|automation|integration_action union), spec (once|recurring w/ IANA-tz rule), enabled,\nnextRunAt (the supervisor's due pointer; null = disabled/exhausted), lastRun {runId,status,at,code}?,\nconsecutiveFailures, autoPausedAt?, createdAt, updatedAt} - _rev CAS updates, authorization\nre-asserted INSIDE the mutator. `schedule_runs` {_id (DETERMINISTIC sha256(scheduleId, plannedFor)\nfor timer fires - the SS4.3.2 insert-as-claim at-most-once guard; random for run-now), scheduleId,\norgId, ownerUserId, status running|ok|failed|blocked|pending|done|dismissed, plannedFor, firedAt?,\nfinishedAt?, trigger auto|manual, detail {code,message}?, automationRunId?, note?, createdAt}.\nTenancy: owner sees own, org-admin sees org (read-only), mutations owner-only; uniform 404s pinned\nbyte-identical by security/schedules-isolation.test.ts. decisions.md 2026-08-17.",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-17 (schedules): TWO new collections (api/src/data/stores.ts). `schedules`\n{_id, orgId, ownerUserId (server-stamped, the fire-time authority), name, description?, target\n(manual|automation|integration_action union), spec (once|recurring w/ IANA-tz rule), enabled,\nnextRunAt (the supervisor's due pointer; null = disabled/exhausted), lastRun {runId,status,at,code}?,\nconsecutiveFailures, autoPausedAt?, createdAt, updatedAt} - _rev CAS updates, authorization\nre-asserted INSIDE the mutator. `schedule_runs` {_id (DETERMINISTIC sha256(scheduleId, plannedFor)\nfor timer fires - the SS4.3.2 insert-as-claim at-most-once guard; random for run-now), scheduleId,\norgId, ownerUserId, status running|ok|failed|blocked|pending|done|dismissed, plannedFor, firedAt?,\nfinishedAt?, trigger auto|manual, detail {code,message}?, automationRunId?, note?, createdAt}.\nTenancy: owner sees own, org-admin sees org (read-only), mutations owner-only; uniform 404s pinned\nbyte-identical by security/schedules-isolation.test.ts. decisions.md 2026-08-17.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-17 (schedules): TWO new collections (api/src/data/stores.ts). `schedules`\n{_id, orgId, ownerUserId (server-stamped, the fire-time authority), name, description?, target\n(manual|automation|integration_action union), spec (once|recurring w/ IANA-tz rule), enabled,\nnextRunAt (the supervisor's due pointer; null = disabled/exhausted), lastRun {runId,status,at,code}?,\nconsecutiveFailures, autoPausedAt?, createdAt, updatedAt} - _rev CAS updates, authorization\nre-asserted INSIDE the mutator. `schedule_runs` {_id (DETERMINISTIC sha256(scheduleId, plannedFor)\nfor timer fires - the SS4.3.2 insert-as-claim at-most-once guard; random for run-now), scheduleId,\norgId, ownerUserId, status running|ok|failed|blocked|pending|done|dismissed, plannedFor, firedAt?,\nfinishedAt?, trigger auto|manual, detail {code,message}?, automationRunId?, note?, createdAt}.\nTenancy: owner sees own, org-admin sees org (read-only), mutations owner-only; uniform 404s pinned\nbyte-identical by security/schedules-isolation.test.ts. decisions.md 2026-08-17.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608180,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260818-p20-recipe-storage",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 11700,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 402.5,
      "seed": 202608181,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755500000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P2.0, discovery -> capture -> replay storage): ONE new collection, one new\nfield, and the boundary between them. `integration_captured_calls` (NEW, api/src/data/stores.ts;\nintegrations/captured-calls-store.ts wraps it): ONE DOCUMENT PER CAPTURED CALL, _id = DETERMINISTIC\nsha256([orgId, integrationKey, actionName, captureId, seq]) - the SS4.3.2 insert-as-claim, so a\nretried append is refused, not duplicated. Row {_id, orgId, integrationKey, actionName, captureId,\nseq, capturedAt, runId?, call {method, url (query values name-redacted), requestHeaderNames[],\nresponseHeaderNames[], status?, requestBody?, responseBody? (both through SecretRegistry + the\nname-pattern leg, capped at 64KB with truncated:true), contentType?, resourceType?, durationMs?}}.\nHEADER VALUES HAVE NO FIELD TO OCCUPY - the input type carries names only. Lifecycle: capture ->\nlearn -> compile -> discardCapture (deleteMany by the four-part key) - the INDEPENDENT lifecycle\nthat earns a second collection, where definition-store.ts rejected one for publish snapshots.\n`integration_definitions`: actions[] gain OPTIONAL `recipe` (the BOUNDED compiled recipe: version,\ngoal, injectedCalls[{method, urlTemplate, headerNames[] NAMES-ONLY, bodyTemplate?, expectShape?,\nidempotent}], scriptedSteps[{locator, action, value?}], lessons[], capturedCallsRef?, compiledAt,\nsupersedes {version, reason}?). WRITTEN ONLY BY integrations/recipe-store.ts: putRecipe mints\nversion 1, supersedeRecipe bumps it and stamps one-hop lineage (the publishSnapshot lineage SHAPE,\nnever that function - its gate is super-admin and its effect is `global`), and a write touches\nneither visibility nor the publication record. NOT caller content: definition-store.create drops any\ncaller-supplied recipe and carries the stored one forward per action name. Never on the wire\n(definition-registry.definitionFromDoc drops it) and never cross-org (publish-scrub.\npackageConfigFromDoc drops it) - a recipe is tenant data even on a `global` row. Tenancy: orgId in\nboth _id derivations, in every query filter, re-checked after every fetch and inside the CAS\nmutator; security/captured-calls-isolation.test.ts + security/recipe-no-values.test.ts.",
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P2.0, discovery -> capture -> replay storage): ONE new collection, one new\nfield, and the boundary between them. `integration_captured_calls` (NEW, api/src/data/stores.ts;\nintegrations/captured-calls-store.ts wraps it): ONE DOCUMENT PER CAPTURED CALL, _id = DETERMINISTIC\nsha256([orgId, integrationKey, actionName, captureId, seq]) - the SS4.3.2 insert-as-claim, so a\nretried append is refused, not duplicated. Row {_id, orgId, integrationKey, actionName, captureId,\nseq, capturedAt, runId?, call {method, url (query values name-redacted), requestHeaderNames[],\nresponseHeaderNames[], status?, requestBody?, responseBody? (both through SecretRegistry + the\nname-pattern leg, capped at 64KB with truncated:true), contentType?, resourceType?, durationMs?}}.\nHEADER VALUES HAVE NO FIELD TO OCCUPY - the input type carries names only. Lifecycle: capture ->\nlearn -> compile -> discardCapture (deleteMany by the four-part key) - the INDEPENDENT lifecycle\nthat earns a second collection, where definition-store.ts rejected one for publish snapshots.\n`integration_definitions`: actions[] gain OPTIONAL `recipe` (the BOUNDED compiled recipe: version,\ngoal, injectedCalls[{method, urlTemplate, headerNames[] NAMES-ONLY, bodyTemplate?, expectShape?,\nidempotent}], scriptedSteps[{locator, action, value?}], lessons[], capturedCallsRef?, compiledAt,\nsupersedes {version, reason}?). WRITTEN ONLY BY integrations/recipe-store.ts: putRecipe mints\nversion 1, supersedeRecipe bumps it and stamps one-hop lineage (the publishSnapshot lineage SHAPE,\nnever that function - its gate is super-admin and its effect is `global`), and a write touches\nneither visibility nor the publication record. NOT caller content: definition-store.create drops any\ncaller-supplied recipe and carries the stored one forward per action name. Never on the wire\n(definition-registry.definitionFromDoc drops it) and never cross-org (publish-scrub.\npackageConfigFromDoc drops it) - a recipe is tenant data even on a `global` row. Tenancy: orgId in\nboth _id derivations, in every query filter, re-checked after every fetch and inside the CAS\nmutator; security/captured-calls-isolation.test.ts + security/recipe-no-values.test.ts.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (P2.0, discovery -> capture -> replay storage): ONE new collection, one new\nfield, and the boundary between them. `integration_captured_calls` (NEW, api/src/data/stores.ts;\nintegrations/captured-calls-store.ts wraps it): ONE DOCUMENT PER CAPTURED CALL, _id = DETERMINISTIC\nsha256([orgId, integrationKey, actionName, captureId, seq]) - the SS4.3.2 insert-as-claim, so a\nretried append is refused, not duplicated. Row {_id, orgId, integrationKey, actionName, captureId,\nseq, capturedAt, runId?, call {method, url (query values name-redacted), requestHeaderNames[],\nresponseHeaderNames[], status?, requestBody?, responseBody? (both through SecretRegistry + the\nname-pattern leg, capped at 64KB with truncated:true), contentType?, resourceType?, durationMs?}}.\nHEADER VALUES HAVE NO FIELD TO OCCUPY - the input type carries names only. Lifecycle: capture ->\nlearn -> compile -> discardCapture (deleteMany by the four-part key) - the INDEPENDENT lifecycle\nthat earns a second collection, where definition-store.ts rejected one for publish snapshots.\n`integration_definitions`: actions[] gain OPTIONAL `recipe` (the BOUNDED compiled recipe: version,\ngoal, injectedCalls[{method, urlTemplate, headerNames[] NAMES-ONLY, bodyTemplate?, expectShape?,\nidempotent}], scriptedSteps[{locator, action, value?}], lessons[], capturedCallsRef?, compiledAt,\nsupersedes {version, reason}?). WRITTEN ONLY BY integrations/recipe-store.ts: putRecipe mints\nversion 1, supersedeRecipe bumps it and stamps one-hop lineage (the publishSnapshot lineage SHAPE,\nnever that function - its gate is super-admin and its effect is `global`), and a write touches\nneither visibility nor the publication record. NOT caller content: definition-store.create drops any\ncaller-supplied recipe and carries the stored one forward per action name. Never on the wire\n(definition-registry.definitionFromDoc drops it) and never cross-org (publish-scrub.\npackageConfigFromDoc drops it) - a recipe is tenant data even on a `global` row. Tenancy: orgId in\nboth _id derivations, in every query filter, re-checked after every fetch and inside the CAS\nmutator; security/captured-calls-isolation.test.ts + security/recipe-no-values.test.ts.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608200,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820-s1-action-evidence",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 12100,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 577.5,
      "seed": 202608201,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755700000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1, integration action EVIDENCE): ONE new collection, and a deliberate\nNON-field. `integration_action_evidence` (NEW, api/src/data/stores.ts; wrapped by\napi/src/integrations/action-evidence-store.ts). `_id` = sha256(JSON([orgId, integrationKey,\nactionName])) - the tuple and NOTHING else, so exactly ONE live row per action exists and each\nvalidated run SUPERSEDES the previous by writing the same id. No runId, no timestamp and no seq in\nthe id: that is what makes the supersede structural rather than a delete somebody has to remember.\nRow: {orgId, integrationKey, actionName, backingType, shape?, validatedAt, evidence}. `evidence` is\na discriminated union - {kind:'api-call', request, response} carrying the executor's OWN redacted\nrequestSummary plus an 8KB-capped response body, or {kind:'automation', runId, status, steps[]}\ncarrying {stepIndex, stepType, screenshotUrl, excerpt} POINTERS (max 50 steps).\n\nWHY IT IS NOT A FIELD ON integration_definitions, which is where it would naturally have gone:\n(1) it would ride publishedSnapshot into every other org - an evidence sample is one tenant's real\nrequest and real response body - and the only thing between it and a cross-org leak would be a\nscrubber remembering to strip it; in its own collection there is nothing to remember, because no\npublish path reads this module. That structural exclusion IS the sanitisation (D5).\n(2) it would race the 16MB document limit and be re-serialised on every CAS of a row every reader\nof every action already touches (the Trap T2 argument integration_captured_calls made).\n\nNOT THE SAME THING AS integration_captured_calls (2026-08-18 note above). Both exist because they\nanswer different questions with opposite lifecycles: captured calls are the UNBOUNDED, MACHINE-\nfacing raw trace a recipe is compiled out of and then DISCARDED (discardCapture is a normal end of\nlife); evidence is the BOUNDED, durable, HUMAN-facing sample the integration detail page renders and\nthe graduation-to-trusted prerequisite reads. Collapsing them would mean either keeping hundreds of\nraw rows alive forever to render one sample, or destroying the sample the moment a recipe compiled.\n\nTENANCY (rule 5): orgId is the FIRST term of the id, is stored on the row, is a term of every\nfilter, and is re-checked on every fetched document. Suite:\napi/tests/security/action-evidence-isolation.test.ts, mutation-verified in both directions (the\npoint-read re-check and the list filter each reddened separately). ONE cross-tenant reader,\n`pinnedRunIdsForRetention`, returns run IDENTIFIERS ONLY and is reachable from the boot sweeper\nalone - the screenshot sweep walks a filesystem tree with no org in it, so 'which runs must this\nsweep spare' cannot be an org-scoped question.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1, integration action EVIDENCE): ONE new collection, and a deliberate\nNON-field. `integration_action_evidence` (NEW, api/src/data/stores.ts; wrapped by\napi/src/integrations/action-evidence-store.ts). `_id` = sha256(JSON([orgId, integrationKey,\nactionName])) - the tuple and NOTHING else, so exactly ONE live row per action exists and each\nvalidated run SUPERSEDES the previous by writing the same id. No runId, no timestamp and no seq in\nthe id: that is what makes the supersede structural rather than a delete somebody has to remember.\nRow: {orgId, integrationKey, actionName, backingType, shape?, validatedAt, evidence}. `evidence` is\na discriminated union - {kind:'api-call', request, response} carrying the executor's OWN redacted\nrequestSummary plus an 8KB-capped response body, or {kind:'automation', runId, status, steps[]}\ncarrying {stepIndex, stepType, screenshotUrl, excerpt} POINTERS (max 50 steps).\n\nWHY IT IS NOT A FIELD ON integration_definitions, which is where it would naturally have gone:\n(1) it would ride publishedSnapshot into every other org - an evidence sample is one tenant's real\nrequest and real response body - and the only thing between it and a cross-org leak would be a\nscrubber remembering to strip it; in its own collection there is nothing to remember, because no\npublish path reads this module. That structural exclusion IS the sanitisation (D5).\n(2) it would race the 16MB document limit and be re-serialised on every CAS of a row every reader\nof every action already touches (the Trap T2 argument integration_captured_calls made).\n\nNOT THE SAME THING AS integration_captured_calls (2026-08-18 note above). Both exist because they\nanswer different questions with opposite lifecycles: captured calls are the UNBOUNDED, MACHINE-\nfacing raw trace a recipe is compiled out of and then DISCARDED (discardCapture is a normal end of\nlife); evidence is the BOUNDED, durable, HUMAN-facing sample the integration detail page renders and\nthe graduation-to-trusted prerequisite reads. Collapsing them would mean either keeping hundreds of\nraw rows alive forever to render one sample, or destroying the sample the moment a recipe compiled.\n\nTENANCY (rule 5): orgId is the FIRST term of the id, is stored on the row, is a term of every\nfilter, and is re-checked on every fetched document. Suite:\napi/tests/security/action-evidence-isolation.test.ts, mutation-verified in both directions (the\npoint-read re-check and the list filter each reddened separately). ONE cross-tenant reader,\n`pinnedRunIdsForRetention`, returns run IDENTIFIERS ONLY and is reachable from the boot sweeper\nalone - the screenshot sweep walks a filesystem tree with no org in it, so 'which runs must this\nsweep spare' cannot be an org-scoped question.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1, integration action EVIDENCE): ONE new collection, and a deliberate\nNON-field. `integration_action_evidence` (NEW, api/src/data/stores.ts; wrapped by\napi/src/integrations/action-evidence-store.ts). `_id` = sha256(JSON([orgId, integrationKey,\nactionName])) - the tuple and NOTHING else, so exactly ONE live row per action exists and each\nvalidated run SUPERSEDES the previous by writing the same id. No runId, no timestamp and no seq in\nthe id: that is what makes the supersede structural rather than a delete somebody has to remember.\nRow: {orgId, integrationKey, actionName, backingType, shape?, validatedAt, evidence}. `evidence` is\na discriminated union - {kind:'api-call', request, response} carrying the executor's OWN redacted\nrequestSummary plus an 8KB-capped response body, or {kind:'automation', runId, status, steps[]}\ncarrying {stepIndex, stepType, screenshotUrl, excerpt} POINTERS (max 50 steps).\n\nWHY IT IS NOT A FIELD ON integration_definitions, which is where it would naturally have gone:\n(1) it would ride publishedSnapshot into every other org - an evidence sample is one tenant's real\nrequest and real response body - and the only thing between it and a cross-org leak would be a\nscrubber remembering to strip it; in its own collection there is nothing to remember, because no\npublish path reads this module. That structural exclusion IS the sanitisation (D5).\n(2) it would race the 16MB document limit and be re-serialised on every CAS of a row every reader\nof every action already touches (the Trap T2 argument integration_captured_calls made).\n\nNOT THE SAME THING AS integration_captured_calls (2026-08-18 note above). Both exist because they\nanswer different questions with opposite lifecycles: captured calls are the UNBOUNDED, MACHINE-\nfacing raw trace a recipe is compiled out of and then DISCARDED (discardCapture is a normal end of\nlife); evidence is the BOUNDED, durable, HUMAN-facing sample the integration detail page renders and\nthe graduation-to-trusted prerequisite reads. Collapsing them would mean either keeping hundreds of\nraw rows alive forever to render one sample, or destroying the sample the moment a recipe compiled.\n\nTENANCY (rule 5): orgId is the FIRST term of the id, is stored on the row, is a term of every\nfilter, and is re-checked on every fetched document. Suite:\napi/tests/security/action-evidence-isolation.test.ts, mutation-verified in both directions (the\npoint-read re-check and the list filter each reddened separately). ONE cross-tenant reader,\n`pinnedRunIdsForRetention`, returns run IDENTIFIERS ONLY and is reachable from the boot sweeper\nalone - the screenshot sweep walks a filesystem tree with no org in it, so 'which runs must this\nsweep spare' cannot be an org-scoped question."
    },
