      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608310,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820c-s1r3-evidence-reconciled-by-owner",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 13460,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 720,
      "seed": 202608311,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755860000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND THREE, correcting the ROUND TWO note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): a row's END OF LIFE is decided by the ROW, not by\nthe write.\n\nWHAT THE NOTE ABOVE GOT WRONG. It says \"there is exactly ONE\" removal path and that\ndiscardEvidenceOfRemovedActions \"deletes EVERY OWNER's row for the dropped action while keeping orgId\nas an exact-match term\". The orgId it kept was input.orgId - the org that WROTE the definition -\nwhile every row in this collection is keyed by the org that RAN the action. integration_definitions\nhas a `global` tier precisely so those are different orgs: a super-admin publishes org A's row,\ndefinition-store.getForActor grants the cross-org tier, a user in org B resolves it, connects THEIR\nOWN credential and runs the action, and the evidence row lands under {orgId: orgB, ownerUserId: uB}.\nOrg A dropping the action then ran a deleteMany filtered on org A, which matched nothing - leaving a\ndurable row of org B's real response body plus, for a {kind:'automation'} sample, a pin that nothing\ncould ever release (an action that resolves for nobody can never be superseded either). The same\nhappens with no definition write at all when setVisibility moves a row global -> org (every consumer\norg loses every action) or org -> private (every peer in the author's own org does).\n\nTHE RULE NOW. A row lives only while its OWNER can still RESOLVE its action.\ndiscardEvidenceOfUnresolvableActions(integrationKey, resolve) reads the rows for that key ACROSS\nTENANTS through ActionEvidenceStore.listOwnerRefsForKey - projected to {orgId, ownerUserId,\nactionName}, so no sample crosses the boundary - groups them by (orgId, ownerUserId), asks\ngetForActor which action names that owner still resolves, and discards the rest through\ndiscardEvidence (the per-row removal primitive, which re-checks org AND owner). It fails towards\nKEEPING: a listing that throws collects nothing, a resolution that throws keeps that owner's rows.\ndefinition-store calls it from BOTH writes that can narrow reach - create(..., 'replace') and\nsetVisibility. actionsDroppedBy is deleted; nothing diffs action sets for evidence any more.\n\nAND THE ROW NOW HAS AN OWNER-DRIVEN ERASURE, WHICH IT DID NOT BEFORE. Deleting the\nintegration_configs row (DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key -> service.ts deleteConfig) discards the\nevidence that credential produced, via discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig: scoped to (orgId,\nintegrationKey) plus either the config's custodian or - for a legacy org-shared config, which carries\nno custodian and is the credential findConfigForOwner hands EVERY member - every owner in the org.\nThis is deliberately not the reconciler: the definition still resolves, so a reconcile keeps the row.\n\nREAD SHAPE: pinnedRunIdsForRetention no longer walks whole documents. It queries\n{'evidence.kind':'automation'} with a projection of {'evidence.kind', 'evidence.runId'} - rows are\nhundreds of KB and grow as orgs x owners x integrations x actions with no TTL, and an unprojected\nfind({}) at boot was a multi-gigabyte materialisation whose OOM abort is not a catchable rejection.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND THREE, correcting the ROUND TWO note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): a row's END OF LIFE is decided by the ROW, not by\nthe write.\n\nWHAT THE NOTE ABOVE GOT WRONG. It says \"there is exactly ONE\" removal path and that\ndiscardEvidenceOfRemovedActions \"deletes EVERY OWNER's row for the dropped action while keeping orgId\nas an exact-match term\". The orgId it kept was input.orgId - the org that WROTE the definition -\nwhile every row in this collection is keyed by the org that RAN the action. integration_definitions\nhas a `global` tier precisely so those are different orgs: a super-admin publishes org A's row,\ndefinition-store.getForActor grants the cross-org tier, a user in org B resolves it, connects THEIR\nOWN credential and runs the action, and the evidence row lands under {orgId: orgB, ownerUserId: uB}.\nOrg A dropping the action then ran a deleteMany filtered on org A, which matched nothing - leaving a\ndurable row of org B's real response body plus, for a {kind:'automation'} sample, a pin that nothing\ncould ever release (an action that resolves for nobody can never be superseded either). The same\nhappens with no definition write at all when setVisibility moves a row global -> org (every consumer\norg loses every action) or org -> private (every peer in the author's own org does).\n\nTHE RULE NOW. A row lives only while its OWNER can still RESOLVE its action.\ndiscardEvidenceOfUnresolvableActions(integrationKey, resolve) reads the rows for that key ACROSS\nTENANTS through ActionEvidenceStore.listOwnerRefsForKey - projected to {orgId, ownerUserId,\nactionName}, so no sample crosses the boundary - groups them by (orgId, ownerUserId), asks\ngetForActor which action names that owner still resolves, and discards the rest through\ndiscardEvidence (the per-row removal primitive, which re-checks org AND owner). It fails towards\nKEEPING: a listing that throws collects nothing, a resolution that throws keeps that owner's rows.\ndefinition-store calls it from BOTH writes that can narrow reach - create(..., 'replace') and\nsetVisibility. actionsDroppedBy is deleted; nothing diffs action sets for evidence any more.\n\nAND THE ROW NOW HAS AN OWNER-DRIVEN ERASURE, WHICH IT DID NOT BEFORE. Deleting the\nintegration_configs row (DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key -> service.ts deleteConfig) discards the\nevidence that credential produced, via discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig: scoped to (orgId,\nintegrationKey) plus either the config's custodian or - for a legacy org-shared config, which carries\nno custodian and is the credential findConfigForOwner hands EVERY member - every owner in the org.\nThis is deliberately not the reconciler: the definition still resolves, so a reconcile keeps the row.\n\nREAD SHAPE: pinnedRunIdsForRetention no longer walks whole documents. It queries\n{'evidence.kind':'automation'} with a projection of {'evidence.kind', 'evidence.runId'} - rows are\nhundreds of KB and grow as orgs x owners x integrations x actions with no TTL, and an unprojected\nfind({}) at boot was a multi-gigabyte materialisation whose OOM abort is not a catchable rejection.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (slice S1 ROUND THREE, correcting the ROUND TWO note above - APPEND-ONLY, so read\nthis one as authoritative where the two disagree): a row's END OF LIFE is decided by the ROW, not by\nthe write.\n\nWHAT THE NOTE ABOVE GOT WRONG. It says \"there is exactly ONE\" removal path and that\ndiscardEvidenceOfRemovedActions \"deletes EVERY OWNER's row for the dropped action while keeping orgId\nas an exact-match term\". The orgId it kept was input.orgId - the org that WROTE the definition -\nwhile every row in this collection is keyed by the org that RAN the action. integration_definitions\nhas a `global` tier precisely so those are different orgs: a super-admin publishes org A's row,\ndefinition-store.getForActor grants the cross-org tier, a user in org B resolves it, connects THEIR\nOWN credential and runs the action, and the evidence row lands under {orgId: orgB, ownerUserId: uB}.\nOrg A dropping the action then ran a deleteMany filtered on org A, which matched nothing - leaving a\ndurable row of org B's real response body plus, for a {kind:'automation'} sample, a pin that nothing\ncould ever release (an action that resolves for nobody can never be superseded either). The same\nhappens with no definition write at all when setVisibility moves a row global -> org (every consumer\norg loses every action) or org -> private (every peer in the author's own org does).\n\nTHE RULE NOW. A row lives only while its OWNER can still RESOLVE its action.\ndiscardEvidenceOfUnresolvableActions(integrationKey, resolve) reads the rows for that key ACROSS\nTENANTS through ActionEvidenceStore.listOwnerRefsForKey - projected to {orgId, ownerUserId,\nactionName}, so no sample crosses the boundary - groups them by (orgId, ownerUserId), asks\ngetForActor which action names that owner still resolves, and discards the rest through\ndiscardEvidence (the per-row removal primitive, which re-checks org AND owner). It fails towards\nKEEPING: a listing that throws collects nothing, a resolution that throws keeps that owner's rows.\ndefinition-store calls it from BOTH writes that can narrow reach - create(..., 'replace') and\nsetVisibility. actionsDroppedBy is deleted; nothing diffs action sets for evidence any more.\n\nAND THE ROW NOW HAS AN OWNER-DRIVEN ERASURE, WHICH IT DID NOT BEFORE. Deleting the\nintegration_configs row (DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key -> service.ts deleteConfig) discards the\nevidence that credential produced, via discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig: scoped to (orgId,\nintegrationKey) plus either the config's custodian or - for a legacy org-shared config, which carries\nno custodian and is the credential findConfigForOwner hands EVERY member - every owner in the org.\nThis is deliberately not the reconciler: the definition still resolves, so a reconcile keeps the row.\n\nREAD SHAPE: pinnedRunIdsForRetention no longer walks whole documents. It queries\n{'evidence.kind':'automation'} with a projection of {'evidence.kind', 'evidence.runId'} - rows are\nhundreds of KB and grow as orgs x owners x integrations x actions with no TTL, and an unprojected\nfind({}) at boot was a multi-gigabyte materialisation whose OOM abort is not a catchable rejection."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608250,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820d-s1r4-evidence-who-may-delete",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 14400,
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1060,
      "height": 752.5,
      "seed": 202608251,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755900000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (d) - S1 ROUND FOUR: integration_action_evidence, who may delete a row.\nAMENDS (c). NO STORED SHAPE CHANGE - the document is byte-identical; what changed is the RULE.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n  api/src/data/stores.ts still documented it as (orgId, integrationKey, actionName) - the SIXTH copy\n  of a claim the previous round's commit says it corrected in five places, and the one a future\n  author reads first because it sits on the collection handle. Corrected there too.\n\nWHO MAY DELETE A ROW, and the rule every one of them obeys: A WRITE BY ONE ORG NEVER DELETES ANOTHER\nORG'S DATA.\n  1 SUPERSEDE        recordEvidence writes the same _id. Releases the previous screenshot pin in the\n                     same write. Unchanged.\n  2 THE READER'S OWN action-executor.ts, on unknown_integration / unknown_action, calls\n                     discardOwnerEvidence({orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName?}). BOTH\n                     tenancy terms are required by the type AND are exact-match query terms; there\n                     is no org-wide arm and no all-owners arm on it at all.\n  3 THE WRITING ORG  evidence-reconcile.reconcileOwnOrgEvidence(orgId, key), bound onto\n                     definition-store's seam and called from create(replace), setVisibility and\n                     publishSnapshot. Reads listOwnerRefsInOrg(orgId, key) - projected to\n                     org+owner+action, no sample - and asks the production resolution per owner.\n  4 THE OWNER        DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence ->\n                     discardEvidence, addressed by the deterministic id over the VERIFIED actor.\n                     Idempotent: nothing to erase is {ok, discarded:false}, never a 404 (which would\n                     also be an existence oracle over a colleague's runs).\n  5 THE CREDENTIAL   deleteConfig -> discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig. The org-shared arm is\n                     {everyOwnerExcept: [...]}, not \"everyone\": findConfigForOwner answers a\n                     member's OWN config row before the custodian-less shared one, so a member\n                     holding their own credential was never served by the deleted row.\n  6 RETENTION        sweepExpiredEvidence at boot: one deleteMany on validatedAt < cutoff (ISO-8601\n                     orders lexicographically, so no document is materialised),\n                     EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90. Every successful run rewrites validatedAt, so an\n                     integration in use never ages out.\n\nWHAT IS DELETED FROM (c): the CROSS-TENANT listing listOwnerRefsForKey(key). A reconciler that could\nsee every tenant's rows is what made a cross-tenant DELETE expressible. pinnedRunIdsForRetention\nremains this collection's ONE cross-tenant reader - run IDENTIFIERS only, to a boot job with no\nactor.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL, RECORDED AS OPEN RATHER THAN CLOSED (findings.md\nevidence-orphan-window-until-the-reader-returns): a reader who never returns keeps their own row for\nup to 90 days after its action stops resolving for them. That is the ACCEPTED side of the trade - an\norphaned row is a bounded retention gap, a deleted row is unrecoverable tenant data, and those costs\nare not comparable.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (d) - S1 ROUND FOUR: integration_action_evidence, who may delete a row.\nAMENDS (c). NO STORED SHAPE CHANGE - the document is byte-identical; what changed is the RULE.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n  api/src/data/stores.ts still documented it as (orgId, integrationKey, actionName) - the SIXTH copy\n  of a claim the previous round's commit says it corrected in five places, and the one a future\n  author reads first because it sits on the collection handle. Corrected there too.\n\nWHO MAY DELETE A ROW, and the rule every one of them obeys: A WRITE BY ONE ORG NEVER DELETES ANOTHER\nORG'S DATA.\n  1 SUPERSEDE        recordEvidence writes the same _id. Releases the previous screenshot pin in the\n                     same write. Unchanged.\n  2 THE READER'S OWN action-executor.ts, on unknown_integration / unknown_action, calls\n                     discardOwnerEvidence({orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName?}). BOTH\n                     tenancy terms are required by the type AND are exact-match query terms; there\n                     is no org-wide arm and no all-owners arm on it at all.\n  3 THE WRITING ORG  evidence-reconcile.reconcileOwnOrgEvidence(orgId, key), bound onto\n                     definition-store's seam and called from create(replace), setVisibility and\n                     publishSnapshot. Reads listOwnerRefsInOrg(orgId, key) - projected to\n                     org+owner+action, no sample - and asks the production resolution per owner.\n  4 THE OWNER        DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence ->\n                     discardEvidence, addressed by the deterministic id over the VERIFIED actor.\n                     Idempotent: nothing to erase is {ok, discarded:false}, never a 404 (which would\n                     also be an existence oracle over a colleague's runs).\n  5 THE CREDENTIAL   deleteConfig -> discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig. The org-shared arm is\n                     {everyOwnerExcept: [...]}, not \"everyone\": findConfigForOwner answers a\n                     member's OWN config row before the custodian-less shared one, so a member\n                     holding their own credential was never served by the deleted row.\n  6 RETENTION        sweepExpiredEvidence at boot: one deleteMany on validatedAt < cutoff (ISO-8601\n                     orders lexicographically, so no document is materialised),\n                     EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90. Every successful run rewrites validatedAt, so an\n                     integration in use never ages out.\n\nWHAT IS DELETED FROM (c): the CROSS-TENANT listing listOwnerRefsForKey(key). A reconciler that could\nsee every tenant's rows is what made a cross-tenant DELETE expressible. pinnedRunIdsForRetention\nremains this collection's ONE cross-tenant reader - run IDENTIFIERS only, to a boot job with no\nactor.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL, RECORDED AS OPEN RATHER THAN CLOSED (findings.md\nevidence-orphan-window-until-the-reader-returns): a reader who never returns keeps their own row for\nup to 90 days after its action stops resolving for them. That is the ACCEPTED side of the trade - an\norphaned row is a bounded retention gap, a deleted row is unrecoverable tenant data, and those costs\nare not comparable.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (d) - S1 ROUND FOUR: integration_action_evidence, who may delete a row.\nAMENDS (c). NO STORED SHAPE CHANGE - the document is byte-identical; what changed is the RULE.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n  api/src/data/stores.ts still documented it as (orgId, integrationKey, actionName) - the SIXTH copy\n  of a claim the previous round's commit says it corrected in five places, and the one a future\n  author reads first because it sits on the collection handle. Corrected there too.\n\nWHO MAY DELETE A ROW, and the rule every one of them obeys: A WRITE BY ONE ORG NEVER DELETES ANOTHER\nORG'S DATA.\n  1 SUPERSEDE        recordEvidence writes the same _id. Releases the previous screenshot pin in the\n                     same write. Unchanged.\n  2 THE READER'S OWN action-executor.ts, on unknown_integration / unknown_action, calls\n                     discardOwnerEvidence({orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName?}). BOTH\n                     tenancy terms are required by the type AND are exact-match query terms; there\n                     is no org-wide arm and no all-owners arm on it at all.\n  3 THE WRITING ORG  evidence-reconcile.reconcileOwnOrgEvidence(orgId, key), bound onto\n                     definition-store's seam and called from create(replace), setVisibility and\n                     publishSnapshot. Reads listOwnerRefsInOrg(orgId, key) - projected to\n                     org+owner+action, no sample - and asks the production resolution per owner.\n  4 THE OWNER        DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence ->\n                     discardEvidence, addressed by the deterministic id over the VERIFIED actor.\n                     Idempotent: nothing to erase is {ok, discarded:false}, never a 404 (which would\n                     also be an existence oracle over a colleague's runs).\n  5 THE CREDENTIAL   deleteConfig -> discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig. The org-shared arm is\n                     {everyOwnerExcept: [...]}, not \"everyone\": findConfigForOwner answers a\n                     member's OWN config row before the custodian-less shared one, so a member\n                     holding their own credential was never served by the deleted row.\n  6 RETENTION        sweepExpiredEvidence at boot: one deleteMany on validatedAt < cutoff (ISO-8601\n                     orders lexicographically, so no document is materialised),\n                     EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90. Every successful run rewrites validatedAt, so an\n                     integration in use never ages out.\n\nWHAT IS DELETED FROM (c): the CROSS-TENANT listing listOwnerRefsForKey(key). A reconciler that could\nsee every tenant's rows is what made a cross-tenant DELETE expressible. pinnedRunIdsForRetention\nremains this collection's ONE cross-tenant reader - run IDENTIFIERS only, to a boot job with no\nactor.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL, RECORDED AS OPEN RATHER THAN CLOSED (findings.md\nevidence-orphan-window-until-the-reader-returns): a reader who never returns keeps their own row for\nup to 90 days after its action stops resolving for them. That is the ACCEPTED side of the trade - an\norphaned row is a bounded retention gap, a deleted row is unrecoverable tenant data, and those costs\nare not comparable."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820e-s1r5-evidence-what-ends-a-row",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 12800,
      "width": 747,
      "height": 805.0,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (e) - S1 ROUND FIVE: integration_action_evidence, what ends a row.\nAMENDS (d). NO STORED SHAPE CHANGE - the document is byte-identical; what changed is the RULE, and\nit changed by SUBTRACTION.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nWHAT (d) SAID, AND WHY IT IS RETIRED\n  (d) listed FIVE ways a row ends: the reader's own run collecting its own rows on a refusal, a\n  definition write collecting the writing org's rows, the retention sweep, the owner's DELETE, and\n  deleteConfig's credential erasure. The first two are DELETED. Both answered \"is this action gone?\"\n  synchronously - at one instant, from one vantage - about a row whose lifetime is durable, and both\n  destroyed data that was not stale: the reader-side one on a transient blip, the write-time one on\n  a tier flip that was reverted a minute later.\n\nWHAT ENDS A ROW - THREE DURABLE SIGNALS, EXHAUSTIVE\n  1. TIME. sweepExpiredEvidence (boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90) deletes every row whose\n     validatedAt is older than the cutoff. ONE deleteMany, no materialisation - validatedAt is\n     ISO-8601 and orders lexicographically. It runs BEFORE the pin read, so an expiring row releases\n     its screenshot pin on the SAME boot. THIS IS THE COLLECTOR NOW, not a backstop behind one, and\n     its virtue is that no vantage has to be right about anything.\n  2. THE OWNER. discardEvidence, behind DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence\n     (auth 'user', idempotent, key built from the VERIFIED actor and hashed into the deterministic\n     _id, then re-checked against the stored org + owner). Plus discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig\n     on deleteConfig - the same durable signal one step out, with its two arms unchanged:\n     { userId } for an owner-stamped config, { everyOwnerExcept: [...] } for a legacy org-shared one.\n     It is now the WIDEST delete in the module and carries a full Rule 5 isolation describe.\n  3. A NEWER SAMPLE. recordEvidence puts at the same deterministic _id, so a validated run replaces\n     the previous sample and releases its pin in one write.\n\nMETHODS DELETED FROM THE STORE\n  discardOwnerEvidence ... the reader-side removal primitive (round four).\n  listOwnerRefsInOrg ..... the write-time collector's projected listing (round four; itself the\n                            narrowing of round three's cross-tenant listOwnerRefsForKey). NOTHING in\n                            this codebase enumerates who holds a row any more.\n  The ActionEvidenceOwnerRef and OwnerEvidenceScope types go with them: keeping the shapes would\n  keep the deletion expressible without keeping anything that needs it.\n\nTHE CROSS-TENANT READER IS STILL EXACTLY ONE: pinnedRunIdsForRetention, boot-only, run IDENTIFIERS\nonly, bounded by a projection and a kind query term. Its consumer now SKIPS the screenshot sweep when\nthe read fails rather than sweeping with no pins - see 02-module-map (e).\n\nRESIDUAL, STATED AND NOT CLOSED: an orphaned row - and the screenshot pin behind an automation-backed\none - survives up to 90 days unless its owner deletes it. That is wider than (d) claimed and it is\nthe accepted cost: an orphan is bounded, uniform and owner-closable; a wrongly-deleted row is\nsomebody's only copy of a real client name and a real processo number. OPEN in docs/findings.md as\nevidence-orphan-window-until-ttl.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (e) - S1 ROUND FIVE: integration_action_evidence, what ends a row.\nAMENDS (d). NO STORED SHAPE CHANGE - the document is byte-identical; what changed is the RULE, and\nit changed by SUBTRACTION.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nWHAT (d) SAID, AND WHY IT IS RETIRED\n  (d) listed FIVE ways a row ends: the reader's own run collecting its own rows on a refusal, a\n  definition write collecting the writing org's rows, the retention sweep, the owner's DELETE, and\n  deleteConfig's credential erasure. The first two are DELETED. Both answered \"is this action gone?\"\n  synchronously - at one instant, from one vantage - about a row whose lifetime is durable, and both\n  destroyed data that was not stale: the reader-side one on a transient blip, the write-time one on\n  a tier flip that was reverted a minute later.\n\nWHAT ENDS A ROW - THREE DURABLE SIGNALS, EXHAUSTIVE\n  1. TIME. sweepExpiredEvidence (boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90) deletes every row whose\n     validatedAt is older than the cutoff. ONE deleteMany, no materialisation - validatedAt is\n     ISO-8601 and orders lexicographically. It runs BEFORE the pin read, so an expiring row releases\n     its screenshot pin on the SAME boot. THIS IS THE COLLECTOR NOW, not a backstop behind one, and\n     its virtue is that no vantage has to be right about anything.\n  2. THE OWNER. discardEvidence, behind DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence\n     (auth 'user', idempotent, key built from the VERIFIED actor and hashed into the deterministic\n     _id, then re-checked against the stored org + owner). Plus discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig\n     on deleteConfig - the same durable signal one step out, with its two arms unchanged:\n     { userId } for an owner-stamped config, { everyOwnerExcept: [...] } for a legacy org-shared one.\n     It is now the WIDEST delete in the module and carries a full Rule 5 isolation describe.\n  3. A NEWER SAMPLE. recordEvidence puts at the same deterministic _id, so a validated run replaces\n     the previous sample and releases its pin in one write.\n\nMETHODS DELETED FROM THE STORE\n  discardOwnerEvidence ... the reader-side removal primitive (round four).\n  listOwnerRefsInOrg ..... the write-time collector's projected listing (round four; itself the\n                            narrowing of round three's cross-tenant listOwnerRefsForKey). NOTHING in\n                            this codebase enumerates who holds a row any more.\n  The ActionEvidenceOwnerRef and OwnerEvidenceScope types go with them: keeping the shapes would\n  keep the deletion expressible without keeping anything that needs it.\n\nTHE CROSS-TENANT READER IS STILL EXACTLY ONE: pinnedRunIdsForRetention, boot-only, run IDENTIFIERS\nonly, bounded by a projection and a kind query term. Its consumer now SKIPS the screenshot sweep when\nthe read fails rather than sweeping with no pins - see 02-module-map (e).\n\nRESIDUAL, STATED AND NOT CLOSED: an orphaned row - and the screenshot pin behind an automation-backed\none - survives up to 90 days unless its owner deletes it. That is wider than (d) claimed and it is\nthe accepted cost: an orphan is bounded, uniform and owner-closable; a wrongly-deleted row is\nsomebody's only copy of a real client name and a real processo number. OPEN in docs/findings.md as\nevidence-orphan-window-until-ttl.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (e) - S1 ROUND FIVE: integration_action_evidence, what ends a row.\nAMENDS (d). NO STORED SHAPE CHANGE - the document is byte-identical; what changed is the RULE, and\nit changed by SUBTRACTION.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nWHAT (d) SAID, AND WHY IT IS RETIRED\n  (d) listed FIVE ways a row ends: the reader's own run collecting its own rows on a refusal, a\n  definition write collecting the writing org's rows, the retention sweep, the owner's DELETE, and\n  deleteConfig's credential erasure. The first two are DELETED. Both answered \"is this action gone?\"\n  synchronously - at one instant, from one vantage - about a row whose lifetime is durable, and both\n  destroyed data that was not stale: the reader-side one on a transient blip, the write-time one on\n  a tier flip that was reverted a minute later.\n\nWHAT ENDS A ROW - THREE DURABLE SIGNALS, EXHAUSTIVE\n  1. TIME. sweepExpiredEvidence (boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90) deletes every row whose\n     validatedAt is older than the cutoff. ONE deleteMany, no materialisation - validatedAt is\n     ISO-8601 and orders lexicographically. It runs BEFORE the pin read, so an expiring row releases\n     its screenshot pin on the SAME boot. THIS IS THE COLLECTOR NOW, not a backstop behind one, and\n     its virtue is that no vantage has to be right about anything.\n  2. THE OWNER. discardEvidence, behind DELETE /api/v1/integrations/:key/actions/:actionName/evidence\n     (auth 'user', idempotent, key built from the VERIFIED actor and hashed into the deterministic\n     _id, then re-checked against the stored org + owner). Plus discardEvidenceForDisconnectedConfig\n     on deleteConfig - the same durable signal one step out, with its two arms unchanged:\n     { userId } for an owner-stamped config, { everyOwnerExcept: [...] } for a legacy org-shared one.\n     It is now the WIDEST delete in the module and carries a full Rule 5 isolation describe.\n  3. A NEWER SAMPLE. recordEvidence puts at the same deterministic _id, so a validated run replaces\n     the previous sample and releases its pin in one write.\n\nMETHODS DELETED FROM THE STORE\n  discardOwnerEvidence ... the reader-side removal primitive (round four).\n  listOwnerRefsInOrg ..... the write-time collector's projected listing (round four; itself the\n                            narrowing of round three's cross-tenant listOwnerRefsForKey). NOTHING in\n                            this codebase enumerates who holds a row any more.\n  The ActionEvidenceOwnerRef and OwnerEvidenceScope types go with them: keeping the shapes would\n  keep the deletion expressible without keeping anything that needs it.\n\nTHE CROSS-TENANT READER IS STILL EXACTLY ONE: pinnedRunIdsForRetention, boot-only, run IDENTIFIERS\nonly, bounded by a projection and a kind query term. Its consumer now SKIPS the screenshot sweep when\nthe read fails rather than sweeping with no pins - see 02-module-map (e).\n\nRESIDUAL, STATED AND NOT CLOSED: an orphaned row - and the screenshot pin behind an automation-backed\none - survives up to 90 days unless its owner deletes it. That is wider than (d) claimed and it is\nthe accepted cost: an orphan is bounded, uniform and owner-closable; a wrongly-deleted row is\nsomebody's only copy of a real client name and a real processo number. OPEN in docs/findings.md as\nevidence-orphan-window-until-ttl.",
