    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260821f-s1r7-evidence-cut-is-recorded",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 13800,
      "width": 747,
      "height": 647.5,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (f) - S1 ROUND SEVEN: integration_action_evidence, the cut that was silent.\nAMENDS (e). A STORED SHAPE CHANGE, and the first since this collection landed: evidence.truncated on\nan automation row can now actually be true. ADDITIVE - absent still means \"not cut\", which is what\nevery row written so far means.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nWHAT WAS BROKEN, MEASURED END TO END THROUGH THE REAL COLLECTOR, THE REAL STORE AND REAL MONGO\n  A 200-step run stored steps.length = 50 and truncated = undefined - byte-indistinguishable from a\n  complete 50-step run. The step cap is applied TWICE and both copies are 50: collectRunEvidence\n  slices to MAX_STEPS BEFORE the seam, and capEvidence re-tests\n  evidence.steps.length > MAX_EVIDENCE_STEPS on what arrives. The second test therefore compares\n  50 > 50 on every row production writes, so the disjunct was unreachable and no flag was ever set.\n  AutomationEvidence.truncated's docblock, the store header and the store suite header all claimed\n  the opposite (\"recorded, never silent\").\n  AND THE FIXTURE HID IT: the case that looked like coverage handed recordEvidence a hand-built\n  62-step evidence object - a shape the production writer structurally cannot produce.\n\nTHE FIX: THE SIGNAL TRAVELS WITH THE SLICE, because only the slicer can still see the run's length.\n  1 automation/action-evidence.ts .... CollectedRunEvidence.truncated = run.steps.length > MAX_STEPS,\n                                      set in the same statement that slices.\n  2 integrations/action-executor.ts .. RunEvidenceCollector declares truncated; the automation\n                                      capture forwards it onto the AutomationEvidence it builds.\n  3 action-evidence-store.ts ......... capEvidence keeps BOTH disjuncts. evidence.truncated is the\n                                      one on the production path; the length test stays as the\n                                      module's OWN ceiling against a future caller that forgets to\n                                      cap, recorded as unreachable-from-production rather than as\n                                      the mechanism.\n\nWHY A DURABLE ROW MUST SAY IT IS A PREFIX: the row lives EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90 and is what a\nhuman reads before granting `trusted`, which makes an action auto-runnable by achieve. \"These are the\nfirst 50 steps of a longer run\" is part of what is being judged.\n\nPINNED END TO END, NOT AT A SEAM: tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts drives a\n200-step RunRecord through the real collector, the real executor forward and the real store, with a\n50-step control that must carry no flag. Dropping the forward alone reddens only that case - which is\nexactly the mutant six rounds of seam-local suites survived.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (f) - S1 ROUND SEVEN: integration_action_evidence, the cut that was silent.\nAMENDS (e). A STORED SHAPE CHANGE, and the first since this collection landed: evidence.truncated on\nan automation row can now actually be true. ADDITIVE - absent still means \"not cut\", which is what\nevery row written so far means.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nWHAT WAS BROKEN, MEASURED END TO END THROUGH THE REAL COLLECTOR, THE REAL STORE AND REAL MONGO\n  A 200-step run stored steps.length = 50 and truncated = undefined - byte-indistinguishable from a\n  complete 50-step run. The step cap is applied TWICE and both copies are 50: collectRunEvidence\n  slices to MAX_STEPS BEFORE the seam, and capEvidence re-tests\n  evidence.steps.length > MAX_EVIDENCE_STEPS on what arrives. The second test therefore compares\n  50 > 50 on every row production writes, so the disjunct was unreachable and no flag was ever set.\n  AutomationEvidence.truncated's docblock, the store header and the store suite header all claimed\n  the opposite (\"recorded, never silent\").\n  AND THE FIXTURE HID IT: the case that looked like coverage handed recordEvidence a hand-built\n  62-step evidence object - a shape the production writer structurally cannot produce.\n\nTHE FIX: THE SIGNAL TRAVELS WITH THE SLICE, because only the slicer can still see the run's length.\n  1 automation/action-evidence.ts .... CollectedRunEvidence.truncated = run.steps.length > MAX_STEPS,\n                                      set in the same statement that slices.\n  2 integrations/action-executor.ts .. RunEvidenceCollector declares truncated; the automation\n                                      capture forwards it onto the AutomationEvidence it builds.\n  3 action-evidence-store.ts ......... capEvidence keeps BOTH disjuncts. evidence.truncated is the\n                                      one on the production path; the length test stays as the\n                                      module's OWN ceiling against a future caller that forgets to\n                                      cap, recorded as unreachable-from-production rather than as\n                                      the mechanism.\n\nWHY A DURABLE ROW MUST SAY IT IS A PREFIX: the row lives EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90 and is what a\nhuman reads before granting `trusted`, which makes an action auto-runnable by achieve. \"These are the\nfirst 50 steps of a longer run\" is part of what is being judged.\n\nPINNED END TO END, NOT AT A SEAM: tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts drives a\n200-step RunRecord through the real collector, the real executor forward and the real store, with a\n50-step control that must carry no flag. Dropping the forward alone reddens only that case - which is\nexactly the mutant six rounds of seam-local suites survived.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (f) - S1 ROUND SEVEN: integration_action_evidence, the cut that was silent.\nAMENDS (e). A STORED SHAPE CHANGE, and the first since this collection landed: evidence.truncated on\nan automation row can now actually be true. ADDITIVE - absent still means \"not cut\", which is what\nevery row written so far means.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nWHAT WAS BROKEN, MEASURED END TO END THROUGH THE REAL COLLECTOR, THE REAL STORE AND REAL MONGO\n  A 200-step run stored steps.length = 50 and truncated = undefined - byte-indistinguishable from a\n  complete 50-step run. The step cap is applied TWICE and both copies are 50: collectRunEvidence\n  slices to MAX_STEPS BEFORE the seam, and capEvidence re-tests\n  evidence.steps.length > MAX_EVIDENCE_STEPS on what arrives. The second test therefore compares\n  50 > 50 on every row production writes, so the disjunct was unreachable and no flag was ever set.\n  AutomationEvidence.truncated's docblock, the store header and the store suite header all claimed\n  the opposite (\"recorded, never silent\").\n  AND THE FIXTURE HID IT: the case that looked like coverage handed recordEvidence a hand-built\n  62-step evidence object - a shape the production writer structurally cannot produce.\n\nTHE FIX: THE SIGNAL TRAVELS WITH THE SLICE, because only the slicer can still see the run's length.\n  1 automation/action-evidence.ts .... CollectedRunEvidence.truncated = run.steps.length > MAX_STEPS,\n                                      set in the same statement that slices.\n  2 integrations/action-executor.ts .. RunEvidenceCollector declares truncated; the automation\n                                      capture forwards it onto the AutomationEvidence it builds.\n  3 action-evidence-store.ts ......... capEvidence keeps BOTH disjuncts. evidence.truncated is the\n                                      one on the production path; the length test stays as the\n                                      module's OWN ceiling against a future caller that forgets to\n                                      cap, recorded as unreachable-from-production rather than as\n                                      the mechanism.\n\nWHY A DURABLE ROW MUST SAY IT IS A PREFIX: the row lives EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS = 90 and is what a\nhuman reads before granting `trusted`, which makes an action auto-runnable by achieve. \"These are the\nfirst 50 steps of a longer run\" is part of what is being judged.\n\nPINNED END TO END, NOT AT A SEAM: tests/automation/composition-root-action-seam.test.ts drives a\n200-step RunRecord through the real collector, the real executor forward and the real store, with a\n50-step control that must carry no flag. Dropping the forward alone reddens only that case - which is\nexactly the mutant six rounds of seam-local suites survived.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 202608260,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608261,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
