    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260821g-s1r8-evidence-outcome-term",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 14800,
      "width": 747,
      "height": 822.5,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (g) - S1 ROUND EIGHT: integration_action_evidence, whether the run WORKED.\nAMENDS (f). A STORED SHAPE CHANGE, and an ADDITIVE one: the row gains a DERIVED `outcome` term.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nROW: {orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName, backingType, shape?, validatedAt, outcome,\n  evidence}. outcome = 'succeeded' | 'failed', DERIVED IN recordEvidence FROM THE STORED SAMPLE and\n  never asserted by the caller: the 2xx window for {kind:'api-call'} (the same predicate\n  executeHttpAction branches on), RunStatus's ONE success member `completed` for {kind:'automation'},\n  and 'failed' when the status is ABSENT (fail-closed - \"we cannot tell\" is not \"it worked\").\n\nWHAT WAS BROKEN, AND IT WAS NOT THE ROW SHAPE. Deleting one line from action-executor.ts's evidence\n  closure - `if (!automationResult.success) return null;` - left the whole S1 estate green (14 files,\n  258/258, measured twice). runAutomationForAction answers a failed ENGINE run with\n  {success:false, code:'automation_failed', data:{runId, status}} and that runId is REAL, so without\n  the line collectRunEvidence returns the FAILED trace and recordEvidence PUTs it at the SAME _id:\n  the last successful sample superseded by a failure, re-stamped validatedAt:now, and the failed\n  run's screenshots pinned out of the 7-day sweep by the same write.\n  WHY NOTHING SAW IT: the only suite binding the real seams points at an automation that does not\n  exist, whose refusal is `unknown_automation` and carries no `data`, so runIdOf answers undefined\n  and the mutant is a no-op there. The api-call half of the identical property was pinned THREE ways.\n\nAND THE GRADUATION GATE WAS STANDING ON THAT LINE. promoteToTrusted / ValidatedRunEvidence read\n  PRESENCE plus `shape` and carried NO success signal, so \"an action may only graduate on a run that\n  worked\" - the thing that makes an action auto-runnable by achieve - was true only because of a\n  guard at the WRITE SITE. A gate that depends on a guard inside the thing it gates is not a gate.\n  promoteToTrusted now refuses any outcome but 'succeeded', ABSENT included.\n\nWHY DERIVED AND NOT CARRIED: a term the executor passed in would restate the write site's own\n  belief, so a write site that recorded a failure would label it 'succeeded' and the gate would be\n  exactly as dependent as before. outcomeOf reads the bytes that were actually stored.\n  The 'failed' VALUE IS UNREACHABLE FROM PRODUCTION TODAY (both write sites refuse to record a\n  failure) and that is recorded as the point rather than as dead code: the term is what the gate\n  reads if either refusal is ever lost, and it is reachable through recordEvidence, a production API\n  of this store.\n\nPINNED: tests/integrations/action-evidence-capture.test.ts drives a REAL automation, owned by the\n  caller, to automation_failed through the PRODUCTION seam mapping with the real collector and the\n  real store bound - the engine stood in for at its own ActionRunDeps.run seam, writing its run\n  record through the PRODUCTION writer (automationRunStore.create then update) - and asserts the\n  previous successful row survives BYTE-FOR-BYTE (deep equality, so validatedAt and the pin are\n  covered) and that the failed run was never pinned. The outcome term is pinned at three levels:\n  derivation (store), gate (promoteToTrusted), and end to end (trustAuthoredAction).\n\nNO SCHEMA, DESCRIPTOR, ROUTE OR AUTH CLASS MOVES: `outcome` is an internal document field on a\n  collection with no production reader and no response schema, so OpenAPI and the generated\n  cortex-cli are byte-identical and EXPECTED_PENDING_COUNT is unmoved.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (g) - S1 ROUND EIGHT: integration_action_evidence, whether the run WORKED.\nAMENDS (f). A STORED SHAPE CHANGE, and an ADDITIVE one: the row gains a DERIVED `outcome` term.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nROW: {orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName, backingType, shape?, validatedAt, outcome,\n  evidence}. outcome = 'succeeded' | 'failed', DERIVED IN recordEvidence FROM THE STORED SAMPLE and\n  never asserted by the caller: the 2xx window for {kind:'api-call'} (the same predicate\n  executeHttpAction branches on), RunStatus's ONE success member `completed` for {kind:'automation'},\n  and 'failed' when the status is ABSENT (fail-closed - \"we cannot tell\" is not \"it worked\").\n\nWHAT WAS BROKEN, AND IT WAS NOT THE ROW SHAPE. Deleting one line from action-executor.ts's evidence\n  closure - `if (!automationResult.success) return null;` - left the whole S1 estate green (14 files,\n  258/258, measured twice). runAutomationForAction answers a failed ENGINE run with\n  {success:false, code:'automation_failed', data:{runId, status}} and that runId is REAL, so without\n  the line collectRunEvidence returns the FAILED trace and recordEvidence PUTs it at the SAME _id:\n  the last successful sample superseded by a failure, re-stamped validatedAt:now, and the failed\n  run's screenshots pinned out of the 7-day sweep by the same write.\n  WHY NOTHING SAW IT: the only suite binding the real seams points at an automation that does not\n  exist, whose refusal is `unknown_automation` and carries no `data`, so runIdOf answers undefined\n  and the mutant is a no-op there. The api-call half of the identical property was pinned THREE ways.\n\nAND THE GRADUATION GATE WAS STANDING ON THAT LINE. promoteToTrusted / ValidatedRunEvidence read\n  PRESENCE plus `shape` and carried NO success signal, so \"an action may only graduate on a run that\n  worked\" - the thing that makes an action auto-runnable by achieve - was true only because of a\n  guard at the WRITE SITE. A gate that depends on a guard inside the thing it gates is not a gate.\n  promoteToTrusted now refuses any outcome but 'succeeded', ABSENT included.\n\nWHY DERIVED AND NOT CARRIED: a term the executor passed in would restate the write site's own\n  belief, so a write site that recorded a failure would label it 'succeeded' and the gate would be\n  exactly as dependent as before. outcomeOf reads the bytes that were actually stored.\n  The 'failed' VALUE IS UNREACHABLE FROM PRODUCTION TODAY (both write sites refuse to record a\n  failure) and that is recorded as the point rather than as dead code: the term is what the gate\n  reads if either refusal is ever lost, and it is reachable through recordEvidence, a production API\n  of this store.\n\nPINNED: tests/integrations/action-evidence-capture.test.ts drives a REAL automation, owned by the\n  caller, to automation_failed through the PRODUCTION seam mapping with the real collector and the\n  real store bound - the engine stood in for at its own ActionRunDeps.run seam, writing its run\n  record through the PRODUCTION writer (automationRunStore.create then update) - and asserts the\n  previous successful row survives BYTE-FOR-BYTE (deep equality, so validatedAt and the pin are\n  covered) and that the failed run was never pinned. The outcome term is pinned at three levels:\n  derivation (store), gate (promoteToTrusted), and end to end (trustAuthoredAction).\n\nNO SCHEMA, DESCRIPTOR, ROUTE OR AUTH CLASS MOVES: `outcome` is an internal document field on a\n  collection with no production reader and no response schema, so OpenAPI and the generated\n  cortex-cli are byte-identical and EXPECTED_PENDING_COUNT is unmoved.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (g) - S1 ROUND EIGHT: integration_action_evidence, whether the run WORKED.\nAMENDS (f). A STORED SHAPE CHANGE, and an ADDITIVE one: the row gains a DERIVED `outcome` term.\n\nTHE KEY IS UNCHANGED: _id = sha256(JSON([orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName])).\n\nROW: {orgId, ownerUserId, integrationKey, actionName, backingType, shape?, validatedAt, outcome,\n  evidence}. outcome = 'succeeded' | 'failed', DERIVED IN recordEvidence FROM THE STORED SAMPLE and\n  never asserted by the caller: the 2xx window for {kind:'api-call'} (the same predicate\n  executeHttpAction branches on), RunStatus's ONE success member `completed` for {kind:'automation'},\n  and 'failed' when the status is ABSENT (fail-closed - \"we cannot tell\" is not \"it worked\").\n\nWHAT WAS BROKEN, AND IT WAS NOT THE ROW SHAPE. Deleting one line from action-executor.ts's evidence\n  closure - `if (!automationResult.success) return null;` - left the whole S1 estate green (14 files,\n  258/258, measured twice). runAutomationForAction answers a failed ENGINE run with\n  {success:false, code:'automation_failed', data:{runId, status}} and that runId is REAL, so without\n  the line collectRunEvidence returns the FAILED trace and recordEvidence PUTs it at the SAME _id:\n  the last successful sample superseded by a failure, re-stamped validatedAt:now, and the failed\n  run's screenshots pinned out of the 7-day sweep by the same write.\n  WHY NOTHING SAW IT: the only suite binding the real seams points at an automation that does not\n  exist, whose refusal is `unknown_automation` and carries no `data`, so runIdOf answers undefined\n  and the mutant is a no-op there. The api-call half of the identical property was pinned THREE ways.\n\nAND THE GRADUATION GATE WAS STANDING ON THAT LINE. promoteToTrusted / ValidatedRunEvidence read\n  PRESENCE plus `shape` and carried NO success signal, so \"an action may only graduate on a run that\n  worked\" - the thing that makes an action auto-runnable by achieve - was true only because of a\n  guard at the WRITE SITE. A gate that depends on a guard inside the thing it gates is not a gate.\n  promoteToTrusted now refuses any outcome but 'succeeded', ABSENT included.\n\nWHY DERIVED AND NOT CARRIED: a term the executor passed in would restate the write site's own\n  belief, so a write site that recorded a failure would label it 'succeeded' and the gate would be\n  exactly as dependent as before. outcomeOf reads the bytes that were actually stored.\n  The 'failed' VALUE IS UNREACHABLE FROM PRODUCTION TODAY (both write sites refuse to record a\n  failure) and that is recorded as the point rather than as dead code: the term is what the gate\n  reads if either refusal is ever lost, and it is reachable through recordEvidence, a production API\n  of this store.\n\nPINNED: tests/integrations/action-evidence-capture.test.ts drives a REAL automation, owned by the\n  caller, to automation_failed through the PRODUCTION seam mapping with the real collector and the\n  real store bound - the engine stood in for at its own ActionRunDeps.run seam, writing its run\n  record through the PRODUCTION writer (automationRunStore.create then update) - and asserts the\n  previous successful row survives BYTE-FOR-BYTE (deep equality, so validatedAt and the pin are\n  covered) and that the failed run was never pinned. The outcome term is pinned at three levels:\n  derivation (store), gate (promoteToTrusted), and end to end (trustAuthoredAction).\n\nNO SCHEMA, DESCRIPTOR, ROUTE OR AUTH CLASS MOVES: `outcome` is an internal document field on a\n  collection with no production reader and no response schema, so OpenAPI and the generated\n  cortex-cli are byte-identical and EXPECTED_PENDING_COUNT is unmoved.",
