    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260821h-s1r9-when-a-row-actually-goes",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 15822.5,
      "width": 747,
      "height": 507.5,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (h) - S1 ROUND NINE: integration_action_evidence, when a row actually goes.\nAMENDS (e), and CORRECTS what (e) and this diagram's retention line meant.\n\nNO STORED FIELD CHANGES. The row shape after (g) is final for this round; this note is about the\nLIFETIME of a row, which every earlier note stated as a number without stating its trigger.\n\nWHAT (e) SAID: \"TIME - sweepExpiredEvidence at boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS (90)\". At boot was ALL\nthere was. No interval, no Mongo TTL index, in a container deployed to stay up (restart:\nunless-stopped, persistent volume). So the real lifetime of a row was:\n\n  min(owner's DELETE, next validated run, credential disconnect, THE NEXT DEPLOY + 90 days)\n\n- and for an automation-backed row the pinnedRunIds exemption rode along, so the run's per-step PNGs\noutlived the 7-day screenshot sweep for exactly as long.\n\nWHAT IT IS NOW: server.ts's startRetentionSweepRail re-enters the sweep every\nRETENTION_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS (6h, unref'd), so the automatic term is\n\n  EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS (90 days) + at most one 6h tick\n\nand the screenshot term is DEFAULT_SCREENSHOT_RETENTION_DAYS (7 days) + at most one tick. Every\ndocument that states either bound now writes it the long way rather than rounding to the number.\n\nTHE DISCONNECT ERASURE HAS THE SAME BACKSTOP, AND HAD NONE. discardEvidenceOfDisconnectedConfig\ncatches everything, returns 0 and warns; nothing retries it. The only thing that ever reached a\nleftover row again was this sweep, so a disconnect erasure that hit a Mongo blip was unbounded too.\n\nSTILL TRUE FROM (e): three durable signals end a row - TIME, THE OWNER, A NEWER SAMPLE - and nothing\nsynchronous decides that a row is over. This note changes when the FIRST of those actually fires.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (h) - S1 ROUND NINE: integration_action_evidence, when a row actually goes.\nAMENDS (e), and CORRECTS what (e) and this diagram's retention line meant.\n\nNO STORED FIELD CHANGES. The row shape after (g) is final for this round; this note is about the\nLIFETIME of a row, which every earlier note stated as a number without stating its trigger.\n\nWHAT (e) SAID: \"TIME - sweepExpiredEvidence at boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS (90)\". At boot was ALL\nthere was. No interval, no Mongo TTL index, in a container deployed to stay up (restart:\nunless-stopped, persistent volume). So the real lifetime of a row was:\n\n  min(owner's DELETE, next validated run, credential disconnect, THE NEXT DEPLOY + 90 days)\n\n- and for an automation-backed row the pinnedRunIds exemption rode along, so the run's per-step PNGs\noutlived the 7-day screenshot sweep for exactly as long.\n\nWHAT IT IS NOW: server.ts's startRetentionSweepRail re-enters the sweep every\nRETENTION_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS (6h, unref'd), so the automatic term is\n\n  EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS (90 days) + at most one 6h tick\n\nand the screenshot term is DEFAULT_SCREENSHOT_RETENTION_DAYS (7 days) + at most one tick. Every\ndocument that states either bound now writes it the long way rather than rounding to the number.\n\nTHE DISCONNECT ERASURE HAS THE SAME BACKSTOP, AND HAD NONE. discardEvidenceOfDisconnectedConfig\ncatches everything, returns 0 and warns; nothing retries it. The only thing that ever reached a\nleftover row again was this sweep, so a disconnect erasure that hit a Mongo blip was unbounded too.\n\nSTILL TRUE FROM (e): three durable signals end a row - TIME, THE OWNER, A NEWER SAMPLE - and nothing\nsynchronous decides that a row is over. This note changes when the FIRST of those actually fires.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-21 (h) - S1 ROUND NINE: integration_action_evidence, when a row actually goes.\nAMENDS (e), and CORRECTS what (e) and this diagram's retention line meant.\n\nNO STORED FIELD CHANGES. The row shape after (g) is final for this round; this note is about the\nLIFETIME of a row, which every earlier note stated as a number without stating its trigger.\n\nWHAT (e) SAID: \"TIME - sweepExpiredEvidence at boot, EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS (90)\". At boot was ALL\nthere was. No interval, no Mongo TTL index, in a container deployed to stay up (restart:\nunless-stopped, persistent volume). So the real lifetime of a row was:\n\n  min(owner's DELETE, next validated run, credential disconnect, THE NEXT DEPLOY + 90 days)\n\n- and for an automation-backed row the pinnedRunIds exemption rode along, so the run's per-step PNGs\noutlived the 7-day screenshot sweep for exactly as long.\n\nWHAT IT IS NOW: server.ts's startRetentionSweepRail re-enters the sweep every\nRETENTION_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS (6h, unref'd), so the automatic term is\n\n  EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS (90 days) + at most one 6h tick\n\nand the screenshot term is DEFAULT_SCREENSHOT_RETENTION_DAYS (7 days) + at most one tick. Every\ndocument that states either bound now writes it the long way rather than rounding to the number.\n\nTHE DISCONNECT ERASURE HAS THE SAME BACKSTOP, AND HAD NONE. discardEvidenceOfDisconnectedConfig\ncatches everything, returns 0 and warns; nothing retries it. The only thing that ever reached a\nleftover row again was this sweep, so a disconnect erasure that hit a Mongo blip was unbounded too.\n\nSTILL TRUE FROM (e): three durable signals end a row - TIME, THE OWNER, A NEWER SAMPLE - and nothing\nsynchronous decides that a row is over. This note changes when the FIRST of those actually fires.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
