    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820-s6-published-snapshot-shape",
      "containerId": null,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 12162.5,
      "width": 831.6,
      "height": 735.0,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 733911409,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 481204906,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787500000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (S6, publish doors): NO new collection and NO new field. What changes is\nWHAT THE FROZEN `publishedSnapshot` MAY CONTAIN, plus one field that starts being written.\n\n1. THE PUBLISHED ACTION IS NOW A WHITELIST. packageConfigFromDoc whitelists the PACKAGE fields and\n   that was read as covering the snapshot. It did not: actionsWithoutRecipes SUBTRACTS `recipe` and\n   copies the rest of the action object through, and IntegrationAction is an open superset - so any\n   other field placed on an action rode into the frozen artifact and out to every organisation.\n   publishableActionOf now enumerates the twelve declared package fields (actionName, description,\n   mutates, argsSchema, returnSchema, httpConfig, automationBinding, backingType, capabilities,\n   transport, posture, authProfile) plus the projected `authoring`. `recipe` is still subtracted\n   first, by the one rule all three boundaries read.\n\n2. `authoring` IS PROJECTED, not carried. DROPPED from the snapshot: authoredBy, trustedBy (user\n   ids of people in the AUTHORING tenant - definitionFromDoc is careful never to tell a cross-org\n   reader which org authored a global row, and naming two of its members inside the actions was the\n   same disclosure by a longer route), goal (the author's prose, and the one free-text field on the\n   artifact the chokepoint model pass never sees - FREE_TEXT_PATHS names skillMd, lessons,\n   config.description and config.credentialGuide only), and verification.checks[].detail.\n   KEPT: state, authoredAt, declaredMutates, shape, trustedAt, verification.{verifiedAt, passed}\n   and checks[].{name, ok}. KEEPING `state` IS LOAD-BEARING: an ABSENT authoring record reads as\n   human-written and therefore TRUSTED (authoringStateOf -> 'none' -> isTrustedAction true), so\n   scrubbing the record wholesale would have published every provisional action to every tenant as\n   one a person had reviewed. `shape` is the integrity tie that keeps a re-authored action reading\n   as provisional wherever it is read.\n   TYPE CHANGE (api-internal, additive): IntegrationActionAuthoring.authoredBy / goal / trustedBy\n   become OPTIONAL - the omission expressed in the type. No stored row changes; nothing reads them.\n\n3. `publishRequest.note` IS WRITTEN FOR THE FIRST TIME. The field has existed since E2 and had no\n   writer. It is free text a person types that LEAVES THE TENANT (a super-admin who is not a member\n   of the org reads it in the queue), so the route scrubs it through the PUBLISH floor\n   (scrubPublishText - the read-path scrub plus the strict credential-line rule plus the blanket\n   literal-secret scan, not the narrower egress scrubSecretText) and caps it at\n   PUBLISH_REQUEST_NOTE_MAX_CHARS = 1000 before the store sees it.\n\n4. D5 HOLDS FROM THIS SIDE. Per-action evidence and per-user feedback live in their own\n   tenant-scoped collections and are NOT fields on the definition document, so promotion carries\n   none by construction. Item 1 is what makes that structural rather than nominal: a field added to\n   an action later cannot reach a snapshot without being opted in.\n   THE OTHER HALF IS NOT THIS DIAGRAM'S TO ASSERT: publishedViewOf spreads the stored doc before\n   overlaying the snapshot's content, so a hypothetical evidence field placed ON the row would ride\n   the in-process cross-org VIEW. The wire projection (definitionFromDoc) is itself a whitelist, so\n   nothing reaches a client - but the store owners must keep both stores off this document.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (S6, publish doors): NO new collection and NO new field. What changes is\nWHAT THE FROZEN `publishedSnapshot` MAY CONTAIN, plus one field that starts being written.\n\n1. THE PUBLISHED ACTION IS NOW A WHITELIST. packageConfigFromDoc whitelists the PACKAGE fields and\n   that was read as covering the snapshot. It did not: actionsWithoutRecipes SUBTRACTS `recipe` and\n   copies the rest of the action object through, and IntegrationAction is an open superset - so any\n   other field placed on an action rode into the frozen artifact and out to every organisation.\n   publishableActionOf now enumerates the twelve declared package fields (actionName, description,\n   mutates, argsSchema, returnSchema, httpConfig, automationBinding, backingType, capabilities,\n   transport, posture, authProfile) plus the projected `authoring`. `recipe` is still subtracted\n   first, by the one rule all three boundaries read.\n\n2. `authoring` IS PROJECTED, not carried. DROPPED from the snapshot: authoredBy, trustedBy (user\n   ids of people in the AUTHORING tenant - definitionFromDoc is careful never to tell a cross-org\n   reader which org authored a global row, and naming two of its members inside the actions was the\n   same disclosure by a longer route), goal (the author's prose, and the one free-text field on the\n   artifact the chokepoint model pass never sees - FREE_TEXT_PATHS names skillMd, lessons,\n   config.description and config.credentialGuide only), and verification.checks[].detail.\n   KEPT: state, authoredAt, declaredMutates, shape, trustedAt, verification.{verifiedAt, passed}\n   and checks[].{name, ok}. KEEPING `state` IS LOAD-BEARING: an ABSENT authoring record reads as\n   human-written and therefore TRUSTED (authoringStateOf -> 'none' -> isTrustedAction true), so\n   scrubbing the record wholesale would have published every provisional action to every tenant as\n   one a person had reviewed. `shape` is the integrity tie that keeps