    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "asbuilt-20260820-s4s5-reuse-ladder",
      "containerId": null,
      "x": 60,
      "y": 12162.5,
      "width": 1040,
      "height": 402.5,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#0e7490",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "seed": 202608201,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 202608202,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1755640000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (S4+S5, the reuse ladder): NO NEW COLLECTION AND NO NEW STORED FIELD - recorded\nas a check made, not a check skipped. The compose rung READS `app_data` through the existing\nCollectionsEngine (plus a new `listCollections(scope)` returning distinct collection NAMES, never a\nrow) and writes nothing; the parametrize rung produces request arguments, which live in the request\nand are persisted nowhere. Nothing is minted: the canonical composed answer leaves the definition\ndocument byte-unchanged, pinned in both the module-level and the contract suites.\n\nWHAT IS NEW IS ON THE WIRE AND ON THE AUDIT TRAIL.\n  shared/src/integrations.ts - AchieveIntegrationGoalResponse, ADDITIVE (Rule 7): `outcome` gains\n  'composed' beside executed/authored/refused, plus five optional fields no older outcome produces -\n  `items` (the narrowed rows, capped at 200), `composition` {collection, where {field, op, value},\n  join {resultField, collectionField}, scanned, matchedCollectionRows, matched, truncated}, `ladder`\n  (AchieveLadderStep[]: rung reuse|parametrize|compose|mint x verdict taken|skipped|refused, so a\n  client can see which rung answered AND what the ones above it decided) and `filledArgs` (argument\n  NAMES a model supplied - names only; the values are in the request that was sent, and this is not a\n  second copy of them). AchieveRefusalCode gains six members; `code` is a free string on the wire, so\n  a client that has never heard of them still reads them as refusals.\n\n  activity_logs - ONE new type: `capability_achieve_compose`, written once per composed answer. An\n  execute already logs itself inside the executor; what is new is that a SECOND data source was read\n  to narrow somebody's answer, so the row records integrationKey, actionName, collection, the\n  predicate's field and op, and the scanned/matched counts. NOT recorded: the goal text, any row, and\n  the value the join keyed on.",
      "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (S4+S5, the reuse ladder): NO NEW COLLECTION AND NO NEW STORED FIELD - recorded\nas a check made, not a check skipped. The compose rung READS `app_data` through the existing\nCollectionsEngine (plus a new `listCollections(scope)` returning distinct collection NAMES, never a\nrow) and writes nothing; the parametrize rung produces request arguments, which live in the request\nand are persisted nowhere. Nothing is minted: the canonical composed answer leaves the definition\ndocument byte-unchanged, pinned in both the module-level and the contract suites.\n\nWHAT IS NEW IS ON THE WIRE AND ON THE AUDIT TRAIL.\n  shared/src/integrations.ts - AchieveIntegrationGoalResponse, ADDITIVE (Rule 7): `outcome` gains\n  'composed' beside executed/authored/refused, plus five optional fields no older outcome produces -\n  `items` (the narrowed rows, capped at 200), `composition` {collection, where {field, op, value},\n  join {resultField, collectionField}, scanned, matchedCollectionRows, matched, truncated}, `ladder`\n  (AchieveLadderStep[]: rung reuse|parametrize|compose|mint x verdict taken|skipped|refused, so a\n  client can see which rung answered AND what the ones above it decided) and `filledArgs` (argument\n  NAMES a model supplied - names only; the values are in the request that was sent, and this is not a\n  second copy of them). AchieveRefusalCode gains six members; `code` is a free string on the wire, so\n  a client that has never heard of them still reads them as refusals.\n\n  activity_logs - ONE new type: `capability_achieve_compose`, written once per composed answer. An\n  execute already logs itself inside the executor; what is new is that a SECOND data source was read\n  to narrow somebody's answer, so the row records integrationKey, actionName, collection, the\n  predicate's field and op, and the scanned/matched counts. NOT recorded: the goal text, any row, and\n  the value the join keyed on.",
      "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-20 (S4+S5, the reuse ladder): NO NEW COLLECTION AND NO NEW STORED FIELD - recorded\nas a check made, not a check skipped. The compose rung READS `app_data` through the existing\nCollectionsEngine (plus a new `listCollections(scope)` returning distinct collection NAMES, never a\nrow) and writes nothing; the parametrize rung produces request arguments, which live in the request\nand are persisted nowhere. Nothing is minted: the canonical composed answer leaves the definition\ndocument byte-unchanged, pinned in both the module-level and the contract suites.\n\nWHAT IS NEW IS ON THE WIRE AND ON THE AUDIT TRAIL.\n  shared/src/integrations.ts - AchieveIntegrationGoalResponse, ADDITIVE (Rule 7): `outcome` gains\n  'composed' beside executed/authored/refused, plus five optional fields no older outcome produces -\n  `items` (the narrowed rows, capped at 200), `composition` {collection, where {field, op, value},\n  join {resultField, collectionField}, scanned, matchedCollectionRows, matched, truncated}, `ladder`\n  (AchieveLadderStep[]: rung reuse|parametrize|compose|mint x verdict taken|skipped|refused, so a\n  client can see which rung answered AND what the ones above it decided) and `filledArgs` (argument\n  NAMES a model supplied - names only; the values are in the request that was sent, and this is not a\n  second copy of them). AchieveRefusalCode gains six members; `code` is a free string on the wire, so\n  a client that has never heard of them still reads them as refusals.\n\n  activity_logs - ONE new type: `capability_achieve_compose`, written once per composed answer. An\n  execute already logs itself inside the executor; what is new is that a SECOND data source was read\n  to narrow somebody's answer, so the row records integrationKey, actionName, collection, the\n  predicate's field and op, and the scanned/matched counts. NOT recorded: the goal text, any row, and\n  the value the join keyed on."
