      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "text": "CORRECTION 2026-08-20d (S4+S5 verification round FOUR) - THE WIRE LOSES THREE CODES; THE STORE IS\nSTILL UNTOUCHED. Supersedes note (c)'s refusal-code list, which was wrong twice over. Journal:\nD-S5-3.\n\nWHAT (c) SAID:  \"AchieveRefusalCode is now exactly four ladder codes - compose_refused,\n                compose_unknown_collection, compose_unshaped_result - plus the pre-existing author\n                codes. Every remaining ladder refusal is decided BEFORE anything runs, about a call\n                the caller has not yet made.\"\nWHAT WAS WRONG: (i) it says FOUR and then lists THREE; (ii) two of those three are decided AFTER\n                the remote call has been made and has SUCCEEDED - the collection read and `rowsOf`\n                both sit downstream of the execute - so what they refused was an answer the product\n                was already holding. The third (`compose_refused`) is decided before the execute,\n                but it ended a call that executed before the ladder existed, which is the same\n                subtraction one step earlier.\n\nWIRE, REMOVED: `compose_refused`, `compose_unknown_collection`, `compose_unshaped_result`.\n  AchieveRefusalCode is now exactly the THIRTEEN author-arm codes that pre-date the ladder:\n  ambiguous_goal, provisional_match, not_custodian, published_row, baseline_package, not_writable,\n  origin_refused, origin_unbound, authoring_unavailable, billing_blocked, authoring_failed,\n  verification_failed, persist_failed. THE LADDER INTRODUCES NO REFUSAL CODE AT ALL - and that\n  count is the honest statement of the invariant the three previous notes only asserted. `code` is\n  a free string on the wire and the enum was never published, so nothing breaks; OpenAPI and the\n  cortex-cli types never carried the enum in the first place (re-generated to prove it).\n\nWIRE, UNCHANGED, AND NOW CARRYING THE WHOLE STORY. When the composition does not apply the response\n  is `outcome: 'executed'` with `result` = the executor's own body, plus the step\n  { rung: 'compose', verdict: 'refused', detail, violations? }. `items` and `composition` are ABSENT\n  on that answer, because nothing was narrowed: a narrowing block on an un-narrowed answer would be\n  the same class of lie as the silent collection cap note (c) fixed.\n\nSTORE: STILL NO NEW COLLECTION, NO NEW STORED FIELD, NO NEW SCOPE KEY - re-checked a fourth time.\n  `app_data` reads still go through the existing CollectionsEngine binding points under\n  `usr.<ownerUserId>`; `listCollections` is still a `distinct` on the same `appId` filter.\n\nAUDIT ROW (`capability_achieve_compose`): unchanged in shape, and still written ONLY when a join\n  really happened. A composition that did not apply writes no row - the truth of what occurred -\n  and the module suite asserts the ABSENCE rather than leaving it to inspection (a mutant that\n  writes the row on a path where nothing was joined reds two tests).\n\nTHE NOT-FOUND ANSWER CARRIES NO PAYLOAD, and that shape is pinned rather than assumed.\n  `AppCollectionRead` has exactly two members: `{ kind: 'rows'; rows }` and a bare\n  `{ kind: 'unknown_collection' }`. There is nowhere for a fact about another tenant to travel, which\n  is what makes the isolation suite's byte-identical comparison (a name another org holds vs a name\n  nobody holds) hold BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by wording. Adding a payload to that member - a\n  `candidates`, a count of other holders - reds the source guard in the module suite.",
      "rawText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-20d (S4+S5 verification round FOUR) - THE WIRE LOSES THREE CODES; THE STORE IS\nSTILL UNTOUCHED. Supersedes note (c)'s refusal-code list, which was wrong twice over. Journal:\nD-S5-3.\n\nWHAT (c) SAID:  \"AchieveRefusalCode is now exactly four ladder codes - compose_refused,\n                compose_unknown_collection, compose_unshaped_result - plus the pre-existing author\n                codes. Every remaining ladder refusal is decided BEFORE anything runs, about a call\n                the caller has not yet made.\"\nWHAT WAS WRONG: (i) it says FOUR and then lists THREE; (ii) two of those three are decided AFTER\n                the remote call has been made and has SUCCEEDED - the collection read and `rowsOf`\n                both sit downstream of the execute - so what they refused was an answer the product\n                was already holding. The third (`compose_refused`) is decided before the execute,\n                but it ended a call that executed before the ladder existed, which is the same\n                subtraction one step earlier.\n\nWIRE, REMOVED: `compose_refused`, `compose_unknown_collection`, `compose_unshaped_result`.\n  AchieveRefusalCode is now exactly the THIRTEEN author-arm codes that pre-date the ladder:\n  ambiguous_goal, provisional_match, not_custodian, published_row, baseline_package, not_writable,\n  origin_refused, origin_unbound, authoring_unavailable, billing_blocked, authoring_failed,\n  verification_failed, persist_failed. THE LADDER INTRODUCES NO REFUSAL CODE AT ALL - and that\n  count is the honest statement of the invariant the three previous notes only asserted. `code` is\n  a free string on the wire and the enum was never published, so nothing breaks; OpenAPI and the\n  cortex-cli types never carried the enum in the first place (re-generated to prove it).\n\nWIRE, UNCHANGED, AND NOW CARRYING THE WHOLE STORY. When the composition does not apply the response\n  is `outcome: 'executed'` with `result` = the executor's own body, plus the step\n  { rung: 'compose', verdict: 'refused', detail, violations? }. `items` and `composition` are ABSENT\n  on that answer, because nothing was narrowed: a narrowing block on an un-narrowed answer would be\n  the same class of lie as the silent collection cap note (c) fixed.\n\nSTORE: STILL NO NEW COLLECTION, NO NEW STORED FIELD, NO NEW SCOPE KEY - re-checked a fourth time.\n  `app_data` reads still go through the existing CollectionsEngine binding points under\n  `usr.<ownerUserId>`; `listCollections` is still a `distinct` on the same `appId` filter.\n\nAUDIT ROW (`capability_achieve_compose`): unchanged in shape, and still written ONLY when a join\n  really happened. A composition that did not apply writes no row - the truth of what occurred -\n  and the module suite asserts the ABSENCE rather than leaving it to inspection (a mutant that\n  writes the row on a path where nothing was joined reds two tests).\n\nTHE NOT-FOUND ANSWER CARRIES NO PAYLOAD, and that shape is pinned rather than assumed.\n  `AppCollectionRead` has exactly two members: `{ kind: 'rows'; rows }` and a bare\n  `{ kind: 'unknown_collection' }`. There is nowhere for a fact about another tenant to travel, which\n  is what makes the isolation suite's byte-identical comparison (a name another org holds vs a name\n  nobody holds) hold BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by wording. Adding a payload to that member - a\n  `candidates`, a count of other holders - reds the source guard in the module suite.",
      "originalText": "CORRECTION 2026-08-20d (S4+S5 verification round FOUR) - THE WIRE LOSES THREE CODES; THE STORE IS\nSTILL UNTOUCHED. Supersedes note (c)'s refusal-code list, which was wrong twice over. Journal:\nD-S5-3.\n\nWHAT (c) SAID:  \"AchieveRefusalCode is now exactly four ladder codes - compose_refused,\n                compose_unknown_collection, compose_unshaped_result - plus the pre-existing author\n                codes. Every remaining ladder refusal is decided BEFORE anything runs, about a call\n                the caller has not yet made.\"\nWHAT WAS WRONG: (i) it says FOUR and then lists THREE; (ii) two of those three are decided AFTER\n                the remote call has been made and has SUCCEEDED - the collection read and `rowsOf`\n                both sit downstream of the execute - so what they refused was an answer the product\n                was already holding. The third (`compose_refused`) is decided before the execute,\n                but it ended a call that executed before the ladder existed, which is the same\n                subtraction one step earlier.\n\nWIRE, REMOVED: `compose_refused`, `compose_unknown_collection`, `compose_unshaped_result`.\n  AchieveRefusalCode is now exactly the THIRTEEN author-arm codes that pre-date the ladder:\n  ambiguous_goal, provisional_match, not_custodian, published_row, baseline_package, not_writable,\n  origin_refused, origin_unbound, authoring_unavailable, billing_blocked, authoring_failed,\n  verification_failed, persist_failed. THE LADDER INTRODUCES NO REFUSAL CODE AT ALL - and that\n  count is the honest statement of the invariant the three previous notes only asserted. `code` is\n  a free string on the wire and the enum was never published, so nothing breaks; OpenAPI and the\n  cortex-cli types never carried the enum in the first place (re-generated to prove it).\n\nWIRE, UNCHANGED, AND NOW CARRYING THE WHOLE STORY. When the composition does not apply the response\n  is `outcome: 'executed'` with `result` = the executor's own body, plus the step\n  { rung: 'compose', verdict: 'refused', detail, violations? }. `items` and `composition` are ABSENT\n  on that answer, because nothing was narrowed: a narrowing block on an un-narrowed answer would be\n  the same class of lie as the silent collection cap note (c) fixed.\n\nSTORE: STILL NO NEW COLLECTION, NO NEW STORED FIELD, NO NEW SCOPE KEY - re-checked a fourth time.\n  `app_data` reads still go through the existing CollectionsEngine binding points under\n  `usr.<ownerUserId>`; `listCollections` is still a `distinct` on the same `appId` filter.\n\nAUDIT ROW (`capability_achieve_compose`): unchanged in shape, and still written ONLY when a join\n  really happened. A composition that did not apply writes no row - the truth of what occurred -\n  and the module suite asserts the ABSENCE rather than leaving it to inspection (a mutant that\n  writes the row on a path where nothing was joined reds two tests).\n\nTHE NOT-FOUND ANSWER CARRIES NO PAYLOAD, and that shape is pinned rather than assumed.\n  `AppCollectionRead` has exactly two members: `{ kind: 'rows'; rows }` and a bare\n  `{ kind: 'unknown_collection' }`. There is nowhere for a fact about another tenant to travel, which\n  is what makes the isolation suite's byte-identical comparison (a name another org holds vs a name\n  nobody holds) hold BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by wording. Adding a payload to that member - a\n  `candidates`, a count of other holders - reds the source guard in the module suite."
